IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb1-nouns`
IMPORT `cb1-part1-application`
IMPORT `cb1-part2-incorporation`
IMPORT `cb1-part3-capacity`
IMPORT `cb1-part4-records`
IMPORT `cb1-part4-isc-register`
IMPORT `cb1-part5-shares`
IMPORT `cb1-part5-own-shares`
IMPORT `cb1-part5-capital-dividends`
IMPORT `cb1-part6-constrained-shares`
IMPORT `cb1-seat`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), sections 1 and 3 to 47 -- WORKED CASES FOR THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30,
-- which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- Each case is a person in the seat -- an incorporator, a director or officer, or a shareholder -- stating the
-- facts they can state to one question of cb1-seat.l4. The expected answer beside each assertion is written
-- from the text of the Act (the section is named in the comment), never copied from what the code printed.
-- There is at least one case for every question, and at least one case that returns an explicit "not covered"
-- value where the question can return one. Dates are written YMD year month day.

§ `Worked cases for the seat -- an incorporator, director, officer or shareholder`

§§ `Whether the Act applies to my corporation (Part I, s 3)`

-- Aisha incorporated her corporation under the Act and it has not been discontinued.
-- s 3(1): the Act applies to every corporation incorporated under it that has not been discontinued.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my body corporate` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Ben's body corporate was continued under the Act and later discontinued under it.
-- s 3(1): "that has not been discontinued under this Act" -- once discontinued, the Act no longer applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the Act apply to my body corporate` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- A body corporate that was neither incorporated nor continued under the Act.
-- s 3(1): the Act reaches only corporations incorporated or continued under it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the Act apply to my body corporate` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Chen asks whether the Winding-up and Restructuring Act applies to his corporation.
-- s 3(3)(b): the Winding-up and Restructuring Act does not apply to a corporation.
#ASSERT `Is a law excluded from applying to my corporation` `the Winding-up and Restructuring Act` FALSE
-- s 3(3)(a.1): the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act does not apply to a corporation.
#ASSERT `Is a law excluded from applying to my corporation` `the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act` FALSE
-- A provision of a Special Act is inconsistent with the Act; Dara's corporation is subject to the Special Act.
-- s 3(3)(c): the provisions of a Special Act that are inconsistent with this Act do not apply.
#ASSERT `Is a law excluded from applying to my corporation` `a provision of a Special Act, as defined in section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act` TRUE
-- s 3(3)(c): a Special Act provision that is not inconsistent is not excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a law excluded from applying to my corporation` `a provision of a Special Act, as defined in section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act` FALSE)
-- s 3(3) names three laws only; any other law is not excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a law excluded from applying to my corporation` `any other law` FALSE)
-- Eli wants his corporation to run a bank, and Fay wants hers to run a restaurant.
-- s 3(4)(a): no corporation shall carry on the business of a bank.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation prohibited from carrying on this kind of business` `the business of a bank`
-- s 3(4)(b).
#ASSERT `Is my corporation prohibited from carrying on this kind of business` `the business of a company or society to which the Insurance Companies Act applies`
-- s 3(4) lists four businesses only.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation prohibited from carrying on this kind of business` `any other business`)
-- Gita's corporation would run a degree-granting educational institution without any authorization.
-- s 3(5): prohibited unless expressly authorized by a federal or provincial agent with degree-granting power.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation prohibited from carrying on a degree-granting educational institution` TRUE FALSE
-- s 3(5): the express authorization lifts the prohibition.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation prohibited from carrying on a degree-granting educational institution` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 3(5): only a degree-granting institution is caught.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation prohibited from carrying on a degree-granting educational institution` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Incorporating (Part II, s 5 to s 9)`

-- Two individuals and no body corporate sign the articles, and the notices have been sent.
-- s 5(1): one or more individuals or bodies corporate may incorporate by signing the articles and complying with s 7.
#ASSERT `May we incorporate a corporation by signing these articles` 2 0 TRUE TRUE
-- s 5(1): a single body corporate may incorporate.
#ASSERT `May we incorporate a corporation by signing these articles` 0 1 TRUE TRUE
-- s 5(1): "one or more" -- nobody signing is not enough.
#ASSERT NOT (`May we incorporate a corporation by signing these articles` 0 0 TRUE TRUE)
-- s 5(1) with s 5(2): one signer who may not incorporate defeats it (fork cb1-F1).
#ASSERT NOT (`May we incorporate a corporation by signing these articles` 2 0 FALSE TRUE)
-- s 5(1): the signers must also comply with s 7.
#ASSERT NOT (`May we incorporate a corporation by signing these articles` 2 0 TRUE FALSE)
-- Hana is 30, not incapable and not bankrupt.
-- s 5(2): at least 18, not incapable, not bankrupt.
#ASSERT `May I as an individual incorporate a corporation` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 5(2)(a): "not less than 18 years of age" -- 18 qualifies.
#ASSERT `May I as an individual incorporate a corporation` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 5(2)(a): 17 is under 18.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I as an individual incorporate a corporation` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 5(2)(b) with the definition of incapable in s 2(1): found under provincial law unable to manage their property, other than by reason of minority.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I as an individual incorporate a corporation` 30 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 2(1) "incapable": a finding by reason of minority does not make an individual incapable.
#ASSERT `May I as an individual incorporate a corporation` 30 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 2(1) "incapable": declared incapable by a court outside Canada.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I as an individual incorporate a corporation` 30 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 5(2)(c): has the status of bankrupt.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I as an individual incorporate a corporation` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Iris checks her articles item by item. A complete set: form, name, province, classes, a number of directors, and nothing restricted.
-- s 6(1)(a) to (f): all that is required is set out.
#ASSERT `Are my articles of incorporation complete` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 6(1)(a): the name of the corporation is missing.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my articles of incorporation complete` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 6(1)(c)(i): two or more classes of shares, but the rights attaching to each class are not set out.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my articles of incorporation complete` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 6(1)(c)(i): the class rights are set out.
#ASSERT `Are my articles of incorporation complete` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 6(1)(c)(ii): a class may be issued in series, but the directors' authority is not set out.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my articles of incorporation complete` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 6(1)(d): shares are to be restricted, but no statement of the restrictions is set out.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my articles of incorporation complete` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 6(1)(e): a minimum and maximum number of directors is only allowed "subject to paragraph 107(a)", which does not allow it here.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my articles of incorporation complete` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 6(1)(e): a minimum and maximum number of directors, where paragraph 107(a) allows it.
#ASSERT `Are my articles of incorporation complete` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 6(1)(f): the corporation is to be restricted in its businesses, but the restrictions are not set out.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my articles of incorporation complete` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Jun asks whether the articles may carry a provision.
-- s 6(2): any provision permitted by the Act or by law to be set out in the by-laws.
#ASSERT `May my articles set out this provision` TRUE
-- s 6(2): a provision that is not permitted in the by-laws is not within the subsection.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my articles set out this provision` FALSE)
-- Kofi's articles require more votes than the Act; Lena's agreement requires more still; Maya wants to remove a director.
-- s 6(3): nothing in the articles or an agreement -- the Act's fraction.
#ASSERT `What fraction of the votes is needed to effect this action` (1 / 2) FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS (1 / 2)
-- s 6(3): the articles require a greater number of votes, so they prevail.
#ASSERT `What fraction of the votes is needed to effect this action` (1 / 2) TRUE (2 / 3) FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS (2 / 3)
-- s 6(3): the unanimous shareholder agreement requires the greatest number, so it prevails.
#ASSERT `What fraction of the votes is needed to effect this action` (1 / 2) TRUE (2 / 3) TRUE (3 / 4) FALSE EQUALS (3 / 4)
-- s 6(4): the articles may not require more than s 109 to remove a director -- the articles' excess is ignored (fork cb1-F2).
#ASSERT `What fraction of the votes is needed to effect this action` (1 / 2) TRUE (3 / 4) FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS (1 / 2)
-- Noor's articles would require two thirds to remove a director; section 109 requires a majority.
-- s 6(4): not a greater number than s 109 requires.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my articles require this fraction of the votes to remove a director` (2 / 3) (1 / 2))
-- s 6(4): the same number is not "a greater number".
#ASSERT `May my articles require this fraction of the votes to remove a director` (1 / 2) (1 / 2)
-- s 6(4): a smaller number is not a greater number.
#ASSERT `May my articles require this fraction of the votes to remove a director` (1 / 3) (1 / 2)
-- Omar has sent the articles but not the notice of directors.
-- s 7: the articles and the documents required by ss 19 and 106.
#ASSERT `Have I as an incorporator sent what the Act requires to the Director` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 7: the notice of directors under s 106 is missing.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I as an incorporator sent what the Act requires to the Director` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 7: the notice of registered office under s 19 is missing.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I as an incorporator sent what the Act requires to the Director` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Pia asks what the Director will do with her articles.
-- s 8(1): on receipt the Director shall issue a certificate.
#ASSERT `What will the Director do on receiving my articles` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Director must issue a certificate of incorporation`
-- s 8(2): the Director may refuse if a notice shows the corporation would not comply with the Act.
#ASSERT `What will the Director do on receiving my articles` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Director may either issue or refuse the certificate of incorporation`
-- s 8(1): the duty arises only on receipt.
#ASSERT `What will the Director do on receiving my articles` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no duty to issue a certificate arises because the Director has not received articles of incorporation`
-- Quinn's certificate of incorporation shows 1 March 2026.
-- s 9: a corporation comes into existence on the date shown in the certificate.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation come into existence on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
-- s 9: it continues to exist after that date.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation come into existence on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2)
-- s 9: it does not exist before the date shown.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation come into existence on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28))

§§ `My corporation's name (Part II, s 10 to s 13)`

-- Rosa checks the words in her corporation's name.
-- s 10(1): "Inc." is the abbreviation of "Incorporated".
#ASSERT `Does my corporation's name contain a required word` "Inc."
-- s 10(1): "Limited" is a listed word.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation's name contain a required word` "Limited"
-- s 10(1): "Company" is not among the listed words.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation's name contain a required word` "Company")
-- s 10(1): no corporate word.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation's name contain a required word` "")
-- Sam's corporation is named Sam Incorporated and he wants to use Sam Inc.
-- s 10(1): either the full or the corresponding abbreviated form.
#ASSERT `May my corporation use and be legally designated by this form of its name` "Inc." "Incorporated"
-- s 10(1): "Ltd." does not correspond to "Incorporated" (fork cb1-F4).
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation use and be legally designated by this form of its name` "Ltd." "Incorporated")
-- s 10(1): the full form itself.
#ASSERT `May my corporation use and be legally designated by this form of its name` "Incorporated" "Incorporated"
-- Tara's name has no corporate word; Ugo's name had "S.C.C."; Vera's continued body corporate was exempted.
-- s 10(1): every corporation.
#ASSERT `Must my corporation's name contain a required word` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 10(1.1): subsection (1) does not apply to a corporation whose name included "Société commerciale canadienne" or "S.C.C." before that subsection came into force.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation's name contain a required word` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 10(2): the Director may exempt a body corporate continued under the Act; this one was exempted.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation's name contain a required word` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 10(2): continued but not exempted -- the duty stands.
#ASSERT `Must my corporation's name contain a required word` FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Ugo's corporation may use "S.C.C."; Wen's corporation may not.
-- s 10(1.1): such a corporation may use "S.C.C.".
#ASSERT `May my corporation use and be designated by the S.C.C. expression` TRUE "S.C.C."
-- s 10(1.1): or the expression "Société commerciale canadienne".
#ASSERT `May my corporation use and be designated by the S.C.C. expression` TRUE "Société commerciale canadienne"
-- s 10(1.1): the saving belongs only to a corporation whose earlier name included the expression.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation use and be designated by the S.C.C. expression` FALSE "S.C.C.")
-- Xiu sets out an English form; Yara a combined English and French form that does not meet the criteria; Zed a prohibited name.
-- s 10(3): an English form.
#ASSERT `May I set out my corporation's name in the articles in this form` `an English form` FALSE FALSE
-- s 10(3): the combined form must meet the prescribed criteria.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I set out my corporation's name in the articles in this form` `a combined English and French form` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 10(3): the combined form meets the prescribed criteria.
#ASSERT `May I set out my corporation's name in the articles in this form` `a combined English and French form` TRUE FALSE
-- s 10(3), "subject to subsection 12(1)": the name is prohibited.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I set out my corporation's name in the articles in this form` `an English form` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 10(3) lists four forms only.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I set out my corporation's name in the articles in this form` `any other form` FALSE FALSE)
-- Amir's articles set out an English form of the name; Bea's do not.
-- s 10(3): the corporation may use and be designated by any such form.
#ASSERT `May my corporation use and be legally designated by a form of its name set out in the articles` `an English form` FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- s 10(3): the form is not set out in the articles.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation use and be legally designated by a form of its name set out in the articles` `an English form` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 10(3): a combined form that fails the criteria cannot be set out, so it cannot be used.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation use and be legally designated by a form of its name set out in the articles` `a combined English and French form` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Cai sets out a Japanese form of the name for use in Tokyo.
-- s 10(4): any language form for use outside Canada.
#ASSERT `May my corporation use a language form of its name outside Canada` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 10(4): the form may be used outside Canada only.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation use a language form of its name outside Canada` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 10(4), "subject to subsection 12(1)": the name is prohibited.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation use a language form of its name outside Canada` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 10(4): the form must be set out in the articles.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation use a language form of its name outside Canada` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Dev asks about an invoice and about a memo.
-- s 10(5): all contracts, invoices, negotiable instruments and orders for goods or services.
#ASSERT `Must my corporation set out its name on this document` `an invoice issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation`
-- s 10(5).
#ASSERT `Must my corporation set out its name on this document` `a contract issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation`
-- s 10(5) lists four kinds of document only.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation set out its name on this document` `any other document`)
-- s 10(5): the name is in legible characters.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation complied with its duty to set out its name on this document` `an invoice issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation` TRUE
-- s 10(5): the name is not legible on the invoice.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation complied with its duty to set out its name on this document` `an invoice issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation` FALSE)
-- Eve's corporation wants to trade as "Eve's Bakery", which contains no corporate word.
-- s 10(6): another name that contains none of the corporate words.
#ASSERT `May my corporation carry on business under another name` "" FALSE
-- s 10(6): the other name contains a corporate word.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation carry on business under another name` "Inc." FALSE)
-- s 10(6), "subject to subsection 12(1)": the other name is prohibited.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation carry on business under another name` "" TRUE)
-- Finn asks the Director to reserve a name for his intended corporation.
-- s 11(1): on request, for an intended corporation or one that intends to change its name.
#ASSERT `May the Director reserve a name for my intended corporation` TRUE TRUE
-- s 11(1): only on request.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Director reserve a name for my intended corporation` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 11(1): only for an intended corporation or a name change.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Director reserve a name for my intended corporation` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 11(1): reserved for the prescribed period; 90 days counted from 1 March 2026 by the keel's convention (F1) is 30 May 2026.
#ASSERT `Until what day is my name reserved` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) 90 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 5 30
-- Gus and his co-incorporators ask for a designating number name.
-- s 11(2): if requested by the incorporators.
#ASSERT `Must the Director give my corporation a designating number name when we ask` TRUE FALSE
-- s 11(2): or by the corporation.
#ASSERT `Must the Director give my corporation a designating number name when we ask` FALSE TRUE
-- s 11(2): only if requested.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director give my corporation a designating number name when we ask` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 11(2): a designating number followed by "Canada" and a corporate word or abbreviation.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's name a designating number name` TRUE "Inc."
-- s 11(2): "Company" is not one of the corporate words.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation's name a designating number name` TRUE "Company")
-- s 11(2): the name must be a designating number followed by "Canada".
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation's name a designating number name` FALSE "Inc.")
-- Hal's corporation has a name that fails the prescribed requirements.
-- s 12(1): prohibited by the regulations.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's name prohibited` TRUE TRUE
-- s 12(1): neither prohibited nor failing the prescribed requirements.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation's name prohibited` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 12(1): "or that does not meet the prescribed requirements".
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's name prohibited` FALSE FALSE
-- Ines's corporation acquired a prohibited name through inadvertence.
-- s 12(2): the corporation has acquired a name that is prohibited by the regulations.
#ASSERT `Can the Director direct my corporation to change its name` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 12(2): the name is not prohibited and meets the prescribed requirements.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Director direct my corporation to change its name` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 12(2): the name does not meet the prescribed requirements.
#ASSERT `Can the Director direct my corporation to change its name` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 12(2): the power arises when the corporation acquires such a name.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Director direct my corporation to change its name` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- Jo's corporation has a designating number as its name.
-- s 12(4): the Director may direct it to change to a name other than a designating number.
#ASSERT `Can the Director direct my corporation to replace its designating number name` TRUE
-- s 12(4): only where the corporation has a designating number as its name.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Director direct my corporation to replace its designating number name` FALSE)
-- Kay acquired her corporation's name because someone undertook to change names.
-- s 12(4.1): the undertaking is not honoured within the period in s 12(5).
#ASSERT `Can the Director direct my corporation to change its name because an undertaking was not honoured` TRUE FALSE
-- s 12(4.1): unless the undertaking is honoured within that period.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Director direct my corporation to change its name because an undertaking was not honoured` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 12(4.1): only where the name was acquired through such an undertaking.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Director direct my corporation to change its name because an undertaking was not honoured` FALSE FALSE)
-- Leo was directed to change his corporation's name and has not.
-- s 12(5): a directive under s 12(2), (4) or (4.1) not followed within the prescribed period.
#ASSERT `Can the Director revoke my corporation's name and assign a name to it` TRUE FALSE
-- s 12(5): the corporation followed the directive in time.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Director revoke my corporation's name and assign a name to it` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 12(5): there is no directive.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Director revoke my corporation's name and assign a name to it` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 12(5): the prescribed period; 30 days counted from 1 March 2026 (F1) ends on 31 March 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must my corporation follow the Director's directive` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) 30 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 31
-- s 12(5): no revocation, so the name is unchanged.
#ASSERT `What is my corporation's name now` "Acme Inc." FALSE "" FALSE "" EQUALS "Acme Inc."
-- s 12(5): until changed in accordance with s 173, the name is the name assigned by the Director.
#ASSERT `What is my corporation's name now` "Acme Inc." TRUE "5001 Canada Inc." FALSE "" EQUALS "5001 Canada Inc."
-- s 12(5): once changed in accordance with s 173, the new name.
#ASSERT `What is my corporation's name now` "Acme Inc." TRUE "5001 Canada Inc." TRUE "Beta Corp." EQUALS "Beta Corp."
-- Mia's corporation had its name revoked and a name assigned.
-- s 13(1): the Director shall issue a certificate of amendment and give notice of the change.
#ASSERT `Will the Director issue a certificate of amendment and give notice after assigning my corporation a name` TRUE
-- s 13(1): only after a name is assigned under s 12(5).
#ASSERT NOT (`Will the Director issue a certificate of amendment and give notice after assigning my corporation a name` FALSE)
-- s 13(2): the articles are amended on the date shown in the certificate.
#ASSERT `Have my corporation's articles been amended by the certificate of amendment on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
-- s 13(2): not before the date shown.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have my corporation's articles been amended by the certificate of amendment on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 31))

§§ `A contract made before the corporation exists (Part II, s 14)`

-- Ned signed a written lease in the name of a corporation that did not yet exist; the corporation has done nothing since; no exemption; no court order.
-- s 14(1): a person who enters into a written contract in the name of a corporation before it exists is personally bound by it and entitled to its benefits.
#ASSERT `Am I personally bound by a contract I made for a corporation before it existed` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The corporation, within a reasonable time after it came into existence, acted so as to signify its intention to be bound.
-- s 14(2)(b): on adoption the person ceases to be bound, except as provided in s 14(3).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I personally bound by a contract I made for a corporation before it existed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- The contract expressly provides that Ned is not bound.
-- s 14(4): if expressly so provided, the person is not in any event bound.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I personally bound by a contract I made for a corporation before it existed` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- The contract was oral.
-- s 14(1) speaks of a written contract only.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I personally bound by a contract I made for a corporation before it existed` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A court ordered, on an application under s 14(3), that Ned is bound even after the corporation adopted the contract.
-- s 14(2)(b) and s 14(3): "except as provided in subsection (3)" -- the court may make any order it thinks fit.
#ASSERT `Am I personally bound by a contract I made for a corporation before it existed` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Olga's corporation adopted the contract within a reasonable time.
-- s 14(2)(a): on adoption the corporation is bound as if it had been a party from the date of the contract.
#ASSERT `Is the corporation bound by the contract it adopted` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 14(2): adoption must be within a reasonable time after the corporation comes into existence.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the corporation bound by the contract it adopted` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 14(2): adoption requires an action or conduct signifying its intention to be bound.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the corporation bound by the contract it adopted` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Pat is a party to a written pre-incorporation contract.
-- s 14(3): a party may apply, whether or not the corporation adopts the contract.
#ASSERT `May I apply to a court for an order about a contract made before the corporation existed` TRUE TRUE
-- s 14(3): only a party to the contract may apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I apply to a court for an order about a contract made before the corporation existed` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 14(3): the contract must be a written contract made before the corporation existed.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I apply to a court for an order about a contract made before the corporation existed` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 14(3): on the application the court may make any order it thinks fit.
#ASSERT `Can a court make an order about my obligations under a contract I made for a corporation before it existed` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 14(3) is "subject to subsection (4)": an express exemption.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a court make an order about my obligations under a contract I made for a corporation before it existed` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 14(3): there is no application by a party.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a court make an order about my obligations under a contract I made for a corporation before it existed` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `What my corporation can do, and what it cannot be said to have done (Part III, s 15 to s 18)`

-- Ada's body is a corporation, and nothing in the Act takes the natural-person powers away for the act she has in mind.
-- s 15(1): a corporation has the capacity and, subject to the Act, the rights, powers and privileges of a natural person.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have the capacity and the rights, powers and privileges of a natural person` TRUE FALSE
-- s 15(1): "subject to this Act" -- a provision of the Act takes the privilege away.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation have the capacity and the rights, powers and privileges of a natural person` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 15(1) speaks of a corporation.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation have the capacity and the rights, powers and privileges of a natural person` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 15(2).
#ASSERT `May my corporation carry on business throughout Canada` TRUE
-- s 15(2) speaks of a corporation.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation carry on business throughout Canada` FALSE)
-- s 15(3): to the extent that the laws of the jurisdiction permit.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have the capacity to act in a jurisdiction outside Canada` TRUE TRUE
-- s 15(3): the foreign law does not permit it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation have the capacity to act in a jurisdiction outside Canada` TRUE FALSE)
-- Bo's directors want to exercise a power that no by-law confers.
-- s 16(1): it is not necessary for a by-law to be passed to confer a power.
#ASSERT `Do the corporation or its directors have this power without a by-law` TRUE FALSE
-- s 16(1): it removes the need for a by-law; a power that exists only because a by-law was passed is not a power held "without a by-law" (the subsection itself confers nothing).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the corporation or its directors have this power without a by-law` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 16(1) removes the need for a by-law; it does not confer a power nobody else confers.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the corporation or its directors have this power without a by-law` FALSE FALSE)
-- Cy's articles restrict the corporation from carrying on a business; Di's corporation would exercise a power contrary to its articles.
-- s 16(2): shall not carry on any business or exercise any power that it is restricted by its articles from carrying on.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation forbidden to carry on this business or exercise this power` TRUE FALSE
-- s 16(2): nor exercise any power in a manner contrary to its articles.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation forbidden to carry on this business or exercise this power` FALSE TRUE
-- s 16(2): neither restriction applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation forbidden to carry on this business or exercise this power` FALSE FALSE)
-- Eddie's corporation transferred property contrary to its articles.
-- s 16(3): no act is invalid by reason only that it is contrary to its articles or the Act.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is an act of my corporation invalid` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 16(3): the act is invalid on another ground, which s 16(3) does not touch.
#ASSERT `Is an act of my corporation invalid` TRUE TRUE
-- s 16(3): nothing makes the act invalid.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is an act of my corporation invalid` FALSE FALSE)
-- Flo is told that a document filed with the Director binds her with notice of its contents.
-- s 17: no person is affected by or deemed to have notice by reason only that the document is filed or available for inspection.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I affected by the contents of a document about a corporation just because it was filed` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 17 does not displace actual notice or knowledge from another source.
#ASSERT `Am I affected by the contents of a document about a corporation just because it was filed` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Gus dealt with the corporation; it now says its articles were not complied with.
-- s 18(1)(a): the corporation may not assert non-compliance against a person dealing with it.
#ASSERT `Is the corporation barred from asserting this against me` `the articles, by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement have not been complied with` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 18(1)(f).
#ASSERT `Is the corporation barred from asserting this against me` `a sale, lease or exchange of property referred to in subsection 189(3) was not authorized` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 18(2): not against a person who has, or ought to have, knowledge by virtue of their relationship to the corporation (a director, for example).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the corporation barred from asserting this against me` `the articles, by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement have not been complied with` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 18(1) protects a person dealing with the corporation or who acquired rights from it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the corporation barred from asserting this against me` `the articles, by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement have not been complied with` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 18(1) lists six assertions only.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the corporation barred from asserting this against me` `any other assertion` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§§ `Registered office, records and who may see them (Part IV, s 19 to s 21)`

-- Hugh's corporation has a registered office in the province its articles name.
-- s 19(1): at all times a registered office in the province specified in the articles.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have the registered office that the Act requires` TRUE TRUE
-- s 19(1): the registered office is in a different province.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation have the registered office that the Act requires` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 19(1): no registered office.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation have the registered office that the Act requires` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 19(2): the notice shall be sent with any articles that designate or change the province.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation sent the notice of registered office with its articles` TRUE TRUE
-- s 19(2): the notice was not sent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation sent the notice of registered office with its articles` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 19(2): the articles neither designate nor change the province, so no notice is due.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation sent the notice of registered office with its articles` FALSE FALSE
-- s 19(3): within the province specified in the articles.
#ASSERT `May the directors change the place and address of the registered office` TRUE
-- s 19(3): a move to another province needs articles that change the province (s 19(2)), not a directors' decision.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors change the place and address of the registered office` FALSE)
-- s 19(4): within fifteen days of the change; 15 days counted from 1 March 2026 (F1) ends on 16 March 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must my corporation send the notice of change of address` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 16
-- s 19(4): the fifteenth day is in time.
#ASSERT `Did my corporation send the notice of change of address in time` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 16)
-- s 19(4): the sixteenth day is late.
#ASSERT NOT (`Did my corporation send the notice of change of address in time` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 17))
-- s 19(4): "the Director shall file it".
#ASSERT `Must the Director file the notice of change of address my corporation sent` TRUE
-- s 19(4): the duty to file is on a notice in the Director's form.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director file the notice of change of address my corporation sent` FALSE)
-- Ivy's corporation keeps the four kinds of record in s 20(1).
-- s 20(1)(a) to (d).
#ASSERT `Does my corporation keep all the records section 20(1) lists` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 20(1)(d): no securities register that complies with s 50.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation keep all the records section 20(1) lists` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 20(1)(a): the articles and by-laws are missing.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation keep all the records section 20(1) lists` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 20(2): adequate accounting records and the directors' minutes and resolutions.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation keep the accounting records and directors' records section 20(2) requires` TRUE TRUE
-- s 20(2): the directors' minutes and resolutions are missing.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation keep the accounting records and directors' records section 20(2) requires` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 20(2.1): six years after the end of the financial year (counted by F1: 31 December 2026 plus six years).
#ASSERT `By what day must my corporation retain its accounting records` (YearMonthDay 2026 12 31) FALSE 0 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2032 12 31
-- s 20(2.1): subject to a longer retention period in another Act -- ten years here.
#ASSERT `By what day must my corporation retain its accounting records` (YearMonthDay 2026 12 31) TRUE 10 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2036 12 31
-- s 20(3): the record is one described in paragraph 20(1)(b) or subsection 20(2).
#ASSERT `Does a record kept before my body corporate was continued count as a record the Act requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 20(3): on continuance "records" includes similar records required by law before it was continued.
#ASSERT `Does a record kept before my body corporate was continued count as a record the Act requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- s 20(3): the body corporate was not continued under the Act.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does a record kept before my body corporate was continued count as a record the Act requires` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 20(4): at the registered office and open to inspection by the directors.
#ASSERT `Are my corporation's directors' and accounting records kept as the Act requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- s 20(4): or at another place the directors think fit.
#ASSERT `Are my corporation's directors' and accounting records kept as the Act requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- s 20(4): the directors cannot inspect them at all reasonable times.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my corporation's directors' and accounting records kept as the Act requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 20(5.1): inspectable from Canada, with technical assistance, and no tax Act requires them to be kept in Canada.
#ASSERT `May my corporation keep its records outside Canada` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- s 20(5.1) is "subject to" the Income Tax Act and other Acts administered by the Minister of National Revenue.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation keep its records outside Canada` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 20(5.1)(a): the records are not available for inspection from Canada.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation keep its records outside Canada` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 20(5.1)(b): the corporation does not provide the technical assistance.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation keep its records outside Canada` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 20(1): at its registered office.
#ASSERT `Are my corporation's corporate records kept at a place the Act permits` `at the registered office of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 20(1): or any other place in Canada designated by the directors.
#ASSERT `Are my corporation's corporate records kept at a place the Act permits` `at another place in Canada designated by the directors` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 20(1): the directors must designate the place.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my corporation's corporate records kept at a place the Act permits` `at a place in Canada that the directors have not designated` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 20(5.1): outside Canada if inspectable from Canada with technical assistance.
#ASSERT `Are my corporation's corporate records kept at a place the Act permits` `at a place outside Canada` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- s 20(5.1): not inspectable from Canada.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my corporation's corporate records kept at a place the Act permits` `at a place outside Canada` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 20(5): the duty arises only if accounting records are kept outside Canada.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation kept the quarterly accounting records in Canada that the Act requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 20(5.1): "despite subsections (1) and (5)" records may be kept outside Canada if inspectable from Canada.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation kept the quarterly accounting records in Canada that the Act requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 20(5): records are kept outside Canada, a tax Act requires them in Canada, and no quarterly records are kept in Canada.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation kept the quarterly accounting records in Canada that the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 20(5): quarterly records adequate to ascertain the financial position are kept in Canada.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation kept the quarterly accounting records in Canada that the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 20(6): without reasonable cause, fails to comply with s 20.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation guilty of an offence for failing to comply with the records section` TRUE FALSE
-- s 20(6): there was reasonable cause.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation guilty of an offence for failing to comply with the records section` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 20(6): no failure to comply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation guilty of an offence for failing to comply with the records section` FALSE FALSE)
-- Jade asks what she may look at, in a corporation that is not a distributing corporation, as a shareholder.
-- s 21(1): shareholders may examine the s 20(1) records and take extracts free of charge.
#ASSERT `What access do I have to the corporation's records` `a shareholder of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may examine the records during the usual business hours and take extracts, free of charge`
-- s 21(1): creditors too.
#ASSERT `What access do I have to the corporation's records` `a creditor of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may examine the records during the usual business hours and take extracts, free of charge`
-- s 21(1): if the corporation is a distributing corporation, any other person on payment of a reasonable fee.
#ASSERT `What access do I have to the corporation's records` `any other person` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may examine the records during the usual business hours and take extracts, on payment of a reasonable fee`
-- s 21(1): any other person has no right where the corporation is not a distributing corporation.
#ASSERT `What access do I have to the corporation's records` `any other person` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `has no right of access under s 21(1)`
-- s 21(1.1): to examine the securities register of a distributing corporation, a request with an affidavit must come first.
#ASSERT `What access do I have to the corporation's records` `a shareholder of the corporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `must first make a request to the corporation or its agent or mandatary, accompanied by an affidavit referred to in subsection 21(7)`
-- s 21(1.1): on receipt of the affidavit the corporation shall allow access to the securities register, and an extract on payment of a reasonable fee.
#ASSERT `What access do I have to the corporation's records` `a shareholder of the corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `may examine the securities register during the usual business hours once the affidavit is received, and have an extract on payment of a reasonable fee`
-- s 21(1.1) applies to a distributing corporation only.
#ASSERT `What access do I have to the corporation's records` `a shareholder of the corporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `may examine the records during the usual business hours and take extracts, free of charge`
-- s 21(2): a shareholder is entitled on request and without charge to one copy.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a free copy of the articles by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement` TRUE TRUE
-- s 21(2): on request.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to a free copy of the articles by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21(2): shareholders only.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to a free copy of the articles by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement` FALSE TRUE)
-- Kim, a shareholder, sends her affidavit on 1 March 2026 and pays the fee.
-- s 21(3): shareholders, on payment of a reasonable fee and on sending the affidavit.
#ASSERT `May I require the corporation to give me a list of its shareholders` `a shareholder of the corporation` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- s 21(3): the fee has not been paid.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I require the corporation to give me a list of its shareholders` `a shareholder of the corporation` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 21(3): the affidavit has not been sent.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I require the corporation to give me a list of its shareholders` `a shareholder of the corporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21(3): any other person only for a distributing corporation.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I require the corporation to give me a list of its shareholders` `any other person` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 21(3): a distributing corporation, any other person.
#ASSERT `May I require the corporation to give me a list of its shareholders` `any other person` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 21(3): within 10 days after the receipt of the affidavit (counted by F1).
#ASSERT `By what day must the corporation give me the list of shareholders` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 11
-- s 21(3): made up to a date not more than 10 days before the date of receipt of the affidavit.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest date the list of shareholders may be made up to` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 19
-- s 21(3): provided on the tenth day, made up to the tenth day before receipt.
#ASSERT `Has the corporation given me the list of shareholders as the Act requires` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 19)
-- s 21(3): provided after the tenth day.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the corporation given me the list of shareholders as the Act requires` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 19))
-- s 21(3): made up to a date more than 10 days before the receipt.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the corporation given me the list of shareholders as the Act requires` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 18))
-- s 21(3): a list made up to the date of receipt is not more than 10 days before it.
#ASSERT `Has the corporation given me the list of shareholders as the Act requires` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
-- s 21(4): by stating in the affidavit that supplemental lists are required, on payment of a reasonable fee.
#ASSERT `May I require supplemental lists of changes in the shareholders` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 21(4): only a person requiring a basic list.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I require supplemental lists of changes in the shareholders` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 21(4): the affidavit must state that supplemental lists are required.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I require supplemental lists of changes in the shareholders` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 21(4): on payment of a reasonable fee.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I require supplemental lists of changes in the shareholders` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- The basic list was furnished on Thursday 5 March 2026.
-- s 21(5)(a): changes before the date the basic list is furnished -- due on the date the basic list is furnished.
#ASSERT `On what day is a supplemental list due to me` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 3) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 5
-- s 21(5)(b): changes after that date -- due on the business day following the day to which the list relates (Friday 6 March, so Monday 9 March).
#ASSERT `On what day is a supplemental list due to me` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 6) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 9
-- s 21(6): a person requiring a basic or supplemental list may also require the holders of options or rights to be included.
#ASSERT `May I also require the list to include holders of options or rights to acquire shares` TRUE
-- s 21(6): only a person requiring a list.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I also require the list to include holders of options or rights to acquire shares` FALSE)
-- s 21(7): an individual applicant states their name and address and the limited-use promise.
#ASSERT `Does my affidavit say what the Act requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- s 21(7)(b) and (8): a body corporate states its name and address for service, and a director or officer makes the affidavit.
#ASSERT `Does my affidavit say what the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 21(7)(b): a body corporate must state its name and address for service.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my affidavit say what the Act requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 21(8): a body corporate's affidavit shall be made by a director or officer.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my affidavit say what the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21(7)(c): the affidavit must state that the lists will not be used except as s 21(9) permits.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my affidavit say what the Act requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 21(7)(a): the name and address of the applicant.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my affidavit say what the Act requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21(9)(a).
#ASSERT `May I use the shareholder list or register information I obtained for this purpose` `an effort to influence the voting of shareholders of the corporation`
-- s 21(9)(b).
#ASSERT `May I use the shareholder list or register information I obtained for this purpose` `an offer to acquire securities of the corporation`
-- s 21(9)(c).
#ASSERT `May I use the shareholder list or register information I obtained for this purpose` `any other matter relating to the affairs of the corporation`
-- s 21(9): not used except in connection with the three listed matters.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I use the shareholder list or register information I obtained for this purpose` `any other use`)
-- s 21(10): without reasonable cause, contravenes s 21.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of an offence for contravening the access section` TRUE FALSE
-- s 21(10): there was reasonable cause.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence for contravening the access section` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 21(10): no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence for contravening the access section` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Individuals with significant control (Part IV, s 21.1 to s 21.4)`

-- Nia's corporation is privately held: not a reporting issuer, not listed, not in a prescribed class.
-- s 21.1(7): section 21.1 does not apply to a reporting issuer, a listed corporation or a member of a prescribed class; Nia's is none of those.
#ASSERT `Must my corporation keep a register of individuals with significant control` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 21.1(7)(a): a reporting issuer.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation keep a register of individuals with significant control` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 21.1(7)(b): securities listed and posted for trading on a designated stock exchange.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation keep a register of individuals with significant control` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21.1(7)(c): a member of a prescribed class.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation keep a register of individuals with significant control` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Oli's register has every item of s 21.1(1); an address for service was provided and is recorded; no other information is prescribed.
-- s 21.1(1)(a) to (f).
#ASSERT `Does my corporation's register of individuals with significant control contain what the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- s 21.1(1)(a)(iii): an address for service was provided to the corporation, but the register does not contain it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation's register of individuals with significant control contain what the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 21.1(1)(a)(iii): "if it has been provided" -- none was provided, so none is required.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation's register of individuals with significant control contain what the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- s 21.1(1)(a.1): the citizenship of each individual.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation's register of individuals with significant control contain what the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 21.1(1)(e): other information is prescribed and the register does not contain it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation's register of individuals with significant control contain what the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 21.1(1)(f): no description of each step taken under s 21.1(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation's register of individuals with significant control contain what the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 21.1(1): the register is not kept at the registered office or another place in Canada designated by the directors.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation's register of individuals with significant control contain what the Act requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 21.1(2)(a): reasonable steps at least once during each financial year.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation taken the steps the Act requires to keep its register up to date` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 21.1(2)(a): no steps this financial year.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation taken the steps the Act requires to keep its register up to date` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 21.1(2)(b): the Director requested the steps and they were not taken on the request.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation taken the steps the Act requires to keep its register up to date` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 21.1(2)(a) and (b): taken during the year and on the Director's request.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation taken the steps the Act requires to keep its register up to date` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 21.1(2)(c): the regulations provide a time and the steps were not taken at it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation taken the steps the Act requires to keep its register up to date` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Pru's corporation became aware of new information on 1 March 2026.
-- s 21.1(3): within 15 days of becoming aware (counted by F1).
#ASSERT `By what day must my corporation record new information in the register` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 16
-- s 21.1(3): the fifteenth day.
#ASSERT `Did my corporation record the information in the register in time` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 16)
-- s 21.1(3): the sixteenth day.
#ASSERT NOT (`Did my corporation record the information in the register in time` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 17))
-- Quin, a shareholder, was asked for information about who controls the corporation.
-- s 21.1(4): reply accurately and completely as soon as feasible.
#ASSERT `Have I as a shareholder complied with the duty to answer the corporation's request for register information` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 21.1(4): the reply was not accurate and complete.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I as a shareholder complied with the duty to answer the corporation's request for register information` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 21.1(4): not as soon as feasible.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I as a shareholder complied with the duty to answer the corporation's request for register information` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21.1(4): the duty arises only if the corporation requests the information.
#ASSERT `Have I as a shareholder complied with the duty to answer the corporation's request for register information` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Rae ceased to be an individual with significant control on 1 March 2026.
-- s 21.1(5): within one year after the sixth anniversary -- the sixth anniversary is 1 March 2032, so the last day is 1 March 2033.
#ASSERT `By what day must the corporation dispose of my personal information in the register` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2033 3 1)
-- s 21.1(5): the period runs from the day the individual ceased; if they have not ceased there is no day.
#ASSERT `By what day must the corporation dispose of my personal information in the register` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21.1(5): "subject to any other Act ... that provides for a longer retention period" -- the Act does not say what then governs, so not covered (finding in NOTES).
#ASSERT `By what day must the corporation dispose of my personal information in the register` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21.1(6): without reasonable cause, contravenes s 21.1.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation guilty of an offence for contravening the register section` TRUE FALSE
-- s 21.1(6): reasonable cause.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation guilty of an offence for contravening the register section` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 21.2: the corporation to which s 21.1 applies took the prescribed steps.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation taken the prescribed steps when it cannot identify anyone with significant control` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 21.2: it could not identify anyone and did not take the prescribed steps.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation taken the prescribed steps when it cannot identify anyone with significant control` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21.2: the duty arises only if it is unable to identify any individuals.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation taken the prescribed steps when it cannot identify anyone with significant control` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 21.21(1)(a): annual information, in the form and within the period the Director fixes.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation sent the Director its annual information from the register` TRUE TRUE
-- s 21.21(1)(a): not sent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation sent the Director its annual information from the register` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21.21(1)(b): within 15 days after the day on which it is recorded (F1).
#ASSERT `By what day must my corporation send the newly recorded information to the Director` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 16
-- s 21.21(1)(b): within 15 days, in the Director's form.
#ASSERT `Did my corporation send the newly recorded information to the Director in time` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 16) TRUE
-- s 21.21(1)(b): late.
#ASSERT NOT (`Did my corporation send the newly recorded information to the Director in time` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 17) TRUE)
-- s 21.21(1)(b): not in the form the Director fixes.
#ASSERT NOT (`Did my corporation send the newly recorded information to the Director in time` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) FALSE)
-- Sol's certificate of incorporation is dated 1 March 2026; the corporation sent the Director its information.
-- s 21.21(2): on or after the date shown on the certificate the corporation shall send the information.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation complied with its duty to send register information on a new certificate` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE
-- s 21.21(2): the duty has arisen and the information was not sent.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation complied with its duty to send register information on a new certificate` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE)
-- s 21.21(2): before the certificate's date the duty has not arisen.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation complied with its duty to send register information on a new certificate` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) FALSE
-- s 21.21(4): without reasonable cause, contravenes subsection 21.21(1) or (2).
#ASSERT `Is my corporation guilty of an offence for not sending register information to the Director` TRUE FALSE
-- s 21.21(4): reasonable cause.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation guilty of an offence for not sending register information to the Director` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 21.3(1): on request.
#ASSERT `Must my corporation disclose the information in its register to the Director when asked` TRUE TRUE
-- s 21.3(1): only on request.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation disclose the information in its register to the Director when asked` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21.3(1): only a corporation to which s 21.1 applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation disclose the information in its register to the Director when asked` FALSE TRUE)
-- Tess is an individual with significant control and asks who may receive the information her corporation sent.
-- s 21.301: the Director may provide it to FINTRAC.
#ASSERT `Can the Director pass on the information my corporation sent about me to this recipient` `the Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada`
-- s 21.302: or to a provincial corporate registry.
#ASSERT `Can the Director pass on the information my corporation sent about me to this recipient` `a provincial corporate registry`
-- s 21.301.
#ASSERT `Can the Director pass on the information my corporation sent about me to this recipient` `an investigative body referred to in subsection 21.31(2)`
-- ss 21.301 and 21.302 name the recipients.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Director pass on the information my corporation sent about me to this recipient` `any other recipient`)
-- s 21.303(1)(a): their name.
#ASSERT `Must the Director make this information about me available to the public` `their name` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 21.303(1)(c): the residential address only if no address for service has been provided.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director make this information about me available to the public` `their residential address` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 21.303(1)(c): no address for service provided.
#ASSERT `Must the Director make this information about me available to the public` `their residential address` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 21.303(2): not for an individual under 18.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director make this information about me available to the public` `their name` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 21.303(2): not for an individual to whom prescribed circumstances apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director make this information about me available to the public` `their name` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21.303(3): the Director has chosen not to make it available.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director make this information about me available to the public` `their name` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 21.303(3)(a): reasonable belief of a serious threat to safety.
#ASSERT `Can the Director choose not to make my information public if I apply` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 21.303(3)(b)(i): the Director is satisfied the individual is incapable.
#ASSERT `Can the Director choose not to make my information public if I apply` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 21.303(3): no ground.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Director choose not to make my information public if I apply` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 21.303(3): only on application.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the Director choose not to make my information public if I apply` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 21.31(1) and (2)(a): any police force.
#ASSERT `Must my corporation give this body a copy of its register or the information it asks for` `a police force` TRUE TRUE
-- s 21.31(2): the investigative bodies are listed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation give this body a copy of its register or the information it asks for` `any other body` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 21.31(1): only a corporation to which s 21.1 applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation give this body a copy of its register or the information it asks for` `a police force` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 21.31(1): once the request is served or deemed received.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation give this body a copy of its register or the information it asks for` `a police force` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21.31(2)(b).
#ASSERT `Is the body that asked for my corporation's register an investigative body` `the Canada Revenue Agency`
-- s 21.31(2)(b).
#ASSERT `Is the body that asked for my corporation's register an investigative body` `a provincial body that has responsibilities similar to those of the Canada Revenue Agency`
-- s 21.31(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the body that asked for my corporation's register an investigative body` `any other body`)
-- s 21.31(3): relevance to a scheduled offence plus suspicion under (a).
#ASSERT `Has the investigative body made a request it was entitled to make` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 21.31(3)(c): suspicion about a non-corporate entity influenced by an individual with significant control.
#ASSERT `Has the investigative body made a request it was entitled to make` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- s 21.31(3): no reasonable grounds to suspect relevance to a scheduled offence.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the investigative body made a request it was entitled to make` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 21.31(3): relevance alone is not enough; one of (a) to (c) is also required.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the investigative body made a request it was entitled to make` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A request was left at the registered office on Monday 2 March 2026.
-- s 21.31(4): served by leaving it at the registered office -- served that day.
#ASSERT `On what day is the request served or deemed received` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2)
-- s 21.31(4): sent by registered mail, deemed received when it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail.
#ASSERT `On what day is the request served or deemed received` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9)
-- s 21.31(4): "unless there are reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation did not receive the request" -- the Act then gives no day.
#ASSERT `On what day is the request served or deemed received` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21.31(4): neither left nor mailed -- no service.
#ASSERT `On what day is the request served or deemed received` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21.31(5): without reasonable cause, contravenes subsection 21.31(1).
#ASSERT `Is my corporation guilty of an offence for not answering an investigative body's request` TRUE FALSE
-- s 21.31(5): reasonable cause.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation guilty of an offence for not answering an investigative body's request` TRUE TRUE)
-- Uri is a director who knowingly acquiesced in the corporation's failure to keep the register.
-- s 21.4(1): whether or not the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted.
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence as a director or officer by allowing the corporation to contravene the register provisions` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 21.4(1): the director did not knowingly authorize, permit or acquiesce.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I commit an offence as a director or officer by allowing the corporation to contravene the register provisions` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 21.4(1): the corporation did not contravene those provisions.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I commit an offence as a director or officer by allowing the corporation to contravene the register provisions` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21.4(1): the person is not a director or officer.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I commit an offence as a director or officer by allowing the corporation to contravene the register provisions` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21.4(2).
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence as a director or officer by recording false or misleading information in the register` TRUE TRUE
-- s 21.4(2): not knowingly.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I commit an offence as a director or officer by recording false or misleading information in the register` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21.4(3).
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence as a director or officer by giving anyone false or misleading information about the register` TRUE TRUE
-- s 21.4(3): not a director or officer.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I commit an offence as a director or officer by giving anyone false or misleading information about the register` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 21.4(4).
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence as a shareholder by knowingly not answering the corporation's request for register information` TRUE TRUE
-- s 21.4(4): not knowing.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I commit an offence as a shareholder by knowingly not answering the corporation's request for register information` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 21.4(5)(a): a fine not exceeding $200,000 on summary conviction.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for an offence under section 21.4` `summary conviction` EQUALS 200000
-- s 21.4(5)(b): a fine not exceeding $1,000,000 on conviction on indictment.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for an offence under section 21.4` `conviction on indictment` EQUALS 1000000
-- s 21.4(5)(a): imprisonment not exceeding two years (24 months).
#ASSERT `What is the longest term of imprisonment I can receive for an offence under section 21.4` `summary conviction` EQUALS JUST 24
-- s 21.4(5)(b): imprisonment not exceeding five years (60 months).
#ASSERT `What is the longest term of imprisonment I can receive for an offence under section 21.4` `conviction on indictment` EQUALS JUST 60

§§ `Form of records, and the corporate seal (Part IV, s 22 and s 23)`

-- Lena's corporation keeps its registers in a bound book and in a database.
-- s 22(1): a bound or loose-leaf form, or a photographic film form.
#ASSERT `May my corporation keep its registers and records in this form` `a bound form` FALSE
-- s 22(1): a data processing system capable of reproducing the information in intelligible written form within a reasonable time.
#ASSERT `May my corporation keep its registers and records in this form` `entered or recorded by a system of mechanical or electronic data processing or any other information storage device` TRUE
-- s 22(1): the system must be capable of reproducing the information in intelligible written form within a reasonable time.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation keep its registers and records in this form` `entered or recorded by a system of mechanical or electronic data processing or any other information storage device` FALSE)
-- s 22(1) lists the permitted forms.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation keep its registers and records in this form` `any other form` TRUE)
-- s 22(2): precautions against loss or destruction, against falsification, and to facilitate detection and correction of inaccuracies.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation taken the precautions the Act requires for its registers and records` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 22(2): no precautions against falsification of entries.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation taken the precautions the Act requires for its registers and records` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 22(2): no precautions against loss or destruction.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation taken the precautions the Act requires for its registers and records` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 22(3): without reasonable cause, contravenes s 22.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of an offence for contravening the form and precautions section` TRUE FALSE
-- s 22(3): reasonable cause.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence for contravening the form and precautions section` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 22(3): no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence for contravening the form and precautions section` FALSE FALSE)
-- Max asks whether his corporation must have a seal.
-- s 23(1): a corporation may adopt a corporate seal and may change it.
#ASSERT `May my corporation adopt and change a corporate seal` TRUE
-- s 23(1) speaks of a corporation.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation adopt and change a corporate seal` FALSE)
-- s 23(1) is permissive ("may adopt"): the Act does not require a seal.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation adopt a corporate seal` TRUE)
-- s 23(2): not invalid merely because a corporate seal is not affixed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a document I signed for the corporation invalid because no corporate seal is on it` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 23(2) does not cure another ground of invalidity.
#ASSERT `Is a document I signed for the corporation invalid because no corporate seal is on it` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 23(2): a sealed document that is valid on other grounds is valid.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a document I signed for the corporation invalid because no corporate seal is on it` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Shares, stated capital, series, pre-emptive rights and options (Part V, s 24 to s 29.1)`

-- Uma checks the form of her shares.
-- s 24(1): registered form, without nominal or par value.
#ASSERT `Is my share in the form the Act requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 24(1): the share has a nominal or par value.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my share in the form the Act requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 24(2): a par value share issued before the body corporate was continued is deemed to be without par value.
#ASSERT `Is my share in the form the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 24(1): the share is not in registered form.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my share in the form the Act requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Vic holds shares in a corporation with a single class of shares.
-- s 24(3)(a).
#ASSERT `As a holder of the only class of shares do I have this right` TRUE `to vote at any meeting of shareholders of the corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 24(3)(b).
#ASSERT `As a holder of the only class of shares do I have this right` TRUE `to receive any dividend declared by the corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 24(3)(c).
#ASSERT `As a holder of the only class of shares do I have this right` TRUE `to receive the remaining property of the corporation on dissolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 24(3) says the rights "include" the three; whether any other right is held it does not say.
#ASSERT `As a holder of the only class of shares do I have this right` TRUE `any other right` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 24(3) applies only where there is one class of shares.
#ASSERT `As a holder of the only class of shares do I have this right` FALSE `to vote at any meeting of shareholders of the corporation` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 24(3): the rights of the holders are equal in all respects.
#ASSERT `Are the rights of the holders of the only class of shares equal in all respects` TRUE TRUE
-- s 24(3): the rights are not equal.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the rights of the holders of the only class of shares equal in all respects` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 24(3) states a requirement of a single class only; with more than one class it is not engaged.
#ASSERT `Are the rights of the holders of the only class of shares equal in all respects` FALSE FALSE
-- Wes's articles provide for two classes.
-- s 24(4)(a) and (b): class rights set out, and each of the three rights attached to at least one class.
#ASSERT `Do my articles meet the requirements for more than one class of shares` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 24(4)(a): the rights of each class are not set out.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do my articles meet the requirements for more than one class of shares` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 24(4)(b): the right to vote is attached to no class.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do my articles meet the requirements for more than one class of shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 24(4)(b): the right to dividends is attached to no class.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do my articles meet the requirements for more than one class of shares` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 24(4)(b): the right to the remaining property is attached to no class.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do my articles meet the requirements for more than one class of shares` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 24(4) applies only if the articles provide for more than one class.
#ASSERT `Do my articles meet the requirements for more than one class of shares` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Xena's directors want to issue shares.
-- s 25(1): as the directors may determine.
#ASSERT `May the directors decide when to whom and for what consideration shares are issued` FALSE FALSE
-- s 25(1): "subject to the articles, the by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement".
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors decide when to whom and for what consideration shares are issued` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 25(1): "and to section 28" -- a pre-emptive right.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors decide when to whom and for what consideration shares are issued` FALSE TRUE)
-- Yuri bought shares that have been issued.
-- s 25(2): shares issued are non-assessable and the holders are not liable.
#ASSERT `Am I as a holder of shares liable to the corporation or its creditors in respect of them` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 25(2) speaks of shares already issued.
#ASSERT `Am I as a holder of shares liable to the corporation or its creditors in respect of them` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Zoe is to be issued shares for various kinds of consideration.
-- s 25(3): fully paid in money.
#ASSERT `May a share be issued for this consideration` `money` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 25(3): "shall not be issued until the consideration ... is fully paid".
#ASSERT NOT (`May a share be issued for this consideration` `money` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 25(3): property not less in value than the fair equivalent of money.
#ASSERT `May a share be issued for this consideration` `property` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 25(3): value less than the fair equivalent of money.
#ASSERT NOT (`May a share be issued for this consideration` `property` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 25(5): a promissory note made by the person to whom the share is issued is not property.
#ASSERT NOT (`May a share be issued for this consideration` `property` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 25(3): past services not less in value than the fair equivalent.
#ASSERT `May a share be issued for this consideration` `past services` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 25(3) allows money, property or past services only.
#ASSERT NOT (`May a share be issued for this consideration` `any other consideration` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 25(4).
#ASSERT `May the directors take this item into account in valuing property or past services` `reasonable charges and expenses of organization and reorganization` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 25(4).
#ASSERT `May the directors take this item into account in valuing property or past services` `payments for property and past services reasonably expected to benefit the corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 25(4) names two items; it does not say whether others may be taken into account.
#ASSERT `May the directors take this item into account in valuing property or past services` `any other item` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 25(5): ordinary property.
#ASSERT `Does this thing count as property when a share is issued for it` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 25(5): a promissory note made by the person to whom a share is issued is not property.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this thing count as property when a share is issued for it` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 25(5): a note made by an arm's-length stranger is outside the exclusion.
#ASSERT `Does this thing count as property when a share is issued for it` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 25(5): not property at all.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does this thing count as property when a share is issued for it` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 26(1).
#ASSERT `Does my corporation maintain a separate stated capital account for each class and series` TRUE
-- s 26(1).
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation maintain a separate stated capital account for each class and series` FALSE)
-- Abe's corporation received $1,000 for new shares.
-- s 26(2): the full amount of the consideration.
#ASSERT `May my corporation add this amount to the stated capital account on an issue of shares` 1000 1000 `any other issue of shares` FALSE
-- s 26(2): the full amount, unless s 26(3) permits less.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation add this amount to the stated capital account on an issue of shares` 1000 800 `any other issue of shares` FALSE)
-- s 26(3)(a)(i): in a non-arm's-length exchange the corporation may add the whole or any part.
#ASSERT `May my corporation add this amount to the stated capital account on an issue of shares` 1000 800 `in exchange for property of a person who immediately before the exchange did not deal with the corporation at arm's length` FALSE
-- s 26(4): not an amount greater than the consideration received.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation add this amount to the stated capital account on an issue of shares` 1000 1200 `in exchange for property of a person who immediately before the exchange did not deal with the corporation at arm's length` FALSE)
-- s 26(3)(a)(iii): arm's-length property with the consent of all concerned.
#ASSERT `May my corporation add this amount to the stated capital account on an issue of shares` 1000 800 `in exchange for property of a person who dealt with the corporation at arm's length, and the person, the corporation and all the holders of shares in the class or series so issued consent to the exchange` TRUE
-- s 26(3)(a)(iii): without the consent of all concerned the full amount applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation add this amount to the stated capital account on an issue of shares` 1000 800 `in exchange for property of a person who dealt with the corporation at arm's length, and the person, the corporation and all the holders of shares in the class or series so issued consent to the exchange` FALSE)
-- s 26(3)(b): an amalgamation agreement or arrangement.
#ASSERT `May my corporation add this amount to the stated capital account on an issue of shares` 1000 600 `pursuant to an agreement referred to in subsection 182(1) or an arrangement referred to in paragraph 192(1)(b) or (c), or to shareholders of an amalgamating body corporate who receive the shares in addition to or instead of securities of the amalgamated body corporate` FALSE
-- Bea proposes to add retained earnings to stated capital.
-- s 26(5): the amount was not received as consideration for shares and the corporation has shares of more than one class or series.
#ASSERT `Must my corporation's addition to a stated capital account be approved by special resolution` FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- s 26(5)(a): the amount was received as consideration for the issue of shares.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation's addition to a stated capital account be approved by special resolution` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 26(5)(b): the corporation has not issued shares of more than one class or series.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation's addition to a stated capital account be approved by special resolution` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 26(5): unless all the shares are not more than two classes of convertible shares referred to in s 39(5).
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation's addition to a stated capital account be approved by special resolution` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 26(5): approved by special resolution -- 67 of 100 votes is not less than two thirds.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation's addition to a stated capital account the approval the Act requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE 67 33 FALSE
-- s 26(5): 66 of 100 votes is less than two thirds.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation's addition to a stated capital account the approval the Act requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE 66 34 FALSE)
-- s 2(1) "special resolution": or signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation's addition to a stated capital account the approval the Act requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE 1 0 TRUE
-- s 26(5): no special resolution is needed for this addition.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation's addition to a stated capital account the approval the Act requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE
-- Cal's corporation was continued under the Act.
-- s 26(6): a continued body corporate may add any consideration received for a share it issued.
#ASSERT `May my corporation add this amount to a stated capital account` `consideration received by a continued body corporate for a share it issued` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 26(6): the first limb belongs to a body corporate that was continued.
#ASSERT `May my corporation add this amount to a stated capital account` `consideration received by a continued body corporate for a share it issued` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 26(6): at any time, subject to s 26(5), an amount credited to a retained earnings or other surplus account.
#ASSERT `May my corporation add this amount to a stated capital account` `an amount credited to a retained earnings or other surplus account` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 26(6) "subject to subsection (5)": the approval that subsection requires is missing.
#ASSERT `May my corporation add this amount to a stated capital account` `an amount credited to a retained earnings or other surplus account` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 26(6) names two amounts; it says nothing of any other.
#ASSERT `May my corporation add this amount to a stated capital account` `any other amount` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 26(7): subsection (2) does not apply to consideration received before the continuance unless the share is issued after it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the full-amount rule of section 26(2) apply to consideration my continued corporation received earlier` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 26(7): the share is issued after the continuance.
#ASSERT `Does the full-amount rule of section 26(2) apply to consideration my continued corporation received earlier` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 26(7): consideration received after the continuance falls under s 26(2).
#ASSERT `Does the full-amount rule of section 26(2) apply to consideration my continued corporation received earlier` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 26(7) applies only to a continued body corporate.
#ASSERT `Does the full-amount rule of section 26(2) apply to consideration my continued corporation received earlier` FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- s 26(8): any amount unpaid on a share issued before the continuance and paid after it shall be added to the stated capital account.
#ASSERT `Must my continued corporation add an amount paid after the continuance to the stated capital account` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 26(8) applies to a continued body corporate.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my continued corporation add an amount paid after the continuance to the stated capital account` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 26(8): the amount must have been paid after the continuance.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my continued corporation add an amount paid after the continuance to the stated capital account` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 26(9): the stated capital is deemed to include the amount that would have been included had the body corporate been incorporated under the Act (fork cb1-F6: a floor).
#ASSERT `What is my continued corporation's stated capital for the solvency tests` TRUE 500 800 EQUALS 800
-- s 26(9): the amount shown in the accounts is greater.
#ASSERT `What is my continued corporation's stated capital for the solvency tests` TRUE 900 800 EQUALS 900
-- s 26(9) applies to a continued body corporate only.
#ASSERT `What is my continued corporation's stated capital for the solvency tests` FALSE 500 800 EQUALS 500
-- s 26(10): in a manner provided in the Act.
#ASSERT `May my corporation reduce its stated capital or a stated capital account in this way` TRUE
-- s 26(10): except in the manner provided in the Act.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation reduce its stated capital or a stated capital account in this way` FALSE)
-- Dee's corporation invests the money it raises and redeems its shares on demand.
-- s 26(12): a distributing corporation that carries on only the business of investing the consideration it receives for its shares, all or substantially all of which are redeemable on demand.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation an open-end mutual fund` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 26(12): it carries on another business.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation an open-end mutual fund` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 26(12): not a distributing corporation.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation an open-end mutual fund` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 26(12): its shares are not redeemable on demand.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation an open-end mutual fund` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 26(11): the stated capital provisions do not apply to an open-end mutual fund.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the stated capital provisions of the Act apply to my corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 26(11): not an open-end mutual fund, so they apply.
#ASSERT `Do the stated capital provisions of the Act apply to my corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Eli's articles authorize series of a class.
-- s 27(1)(a).
#ASSERT `May my articles authorize a class of shares in series in this way` `the articles fix the number of shares in, and determine the designation, rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to the shares of, each series`
-- s 27(1)(b).
#ASSERT `May my articles authorize a class of shares in series in this way` `the articles authorize the directors to fix the number of shares in, and determine the designation, rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to the shares of, each series`
-- s 27(1) allows these two ways only.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my articles authorize a class of shares in series in this way` `any other way`)
-- Fay holds a series of preferred shares; $600 is available against $900 owing to the whole class, of which $300 is owed to her series.
-- s 27(2): all series of the class participate rateably -- 600 x 300/900 = 200.
#ASSERT `How much does my series of shares receive when what is owing is not paid in full` 600 300 900 EQUALS JUST 200
-- s 27(2): paid in full.
#ASSERT `How much does my series of shares receive when what is owing is not paid in full` 900 300 900 EQUALS JUST 300
-- s 27(2): nothing is owing to the class, so no proportion is defined.
#ASSERT `How much does my series of shares receive when what is owing is not paid in full` 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 27(3): no rights attached to a series shall confer a priority over another series of the same class then outstanding.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the rights attached to my series give it priority over another series of the same class` TRUE)
-- s 27(3): no priority conferred.
#ASSERT `May the rights attached to my series give it priority over another series of the same class` FALSE
-- s 27(4): articles of amendment sent before the issue of the series.
#ASSERT `Have the directors sent the articles of amendment designating the series before issuing the shares` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5)
-- s 27(4): sent after the shares were issued.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have the directors sent the articles of amendment designating the series before issuing the shares` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5))
-- s 27(4) binds directors who exercise their authority under paragraph 27(1)(b).
#ASSERT `Have the directors sent the articles of amendment designating the series before issuing the shares` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5)
-- s 27(5).
#ASSERT `Must the Director issue a certificate of amendment for my series of shares` TRUE
-- s 27(5): on receipt of the articles of amendment.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the Director issue a certificate of amendment for my series of shares` FALSE)
-- s 27(6): amended on the date shown in the certificate.
#ASSERT `Have my articles been amended to designate the series on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
-- s 27(6): not before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have my articles been amended to designate the series on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28))
-- Gil is a shareholder in a corporation whose articles provide a pre-emptive right.
-- s 28(1): if the articles so provide.
#ASSERT `Do I as a shareholder have a pre-emptive right in respect of this issue of shares` TRUE `any other issue of shares`
-- s 28(2)(a).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I as a shareholder have a pre-emptive right in respect of this issue of shares` TRUE `shares to be issued for a consideration other than money`)
-- s 28(2)(b).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I as a shareholder have a pre-emptive right in respect of this issue of shares` TRUE `shares to be issued as a share dividend`)
-- s 28(2)(c).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I as a shareholder have a pre-emptive right in respect of this issue of shares` TRUE `shares to be issued pursuant to the exercise of conversion privileges, options or rights previously granted by the corporation`)
-- s 28(1): the right exists only if the articles provide for it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I as a shareholder have a pre-emptive right in respect of this issue of shares` FALSE `any other issue of shares`)
-- s 28(1): in proportion to holdings -- 100 x 10/100 = 10.
#ASSERT `How many of the offered shares do I have a pre-emptive right to acquire` 100 10 100 EQUALS JUST 10
-- s 28(1): 200 x 25/100 = 50.
#ASSERT `How many of the offered shares do I have a pre-emptive right to acquire` 200 25 100 EQUALS JUST 50
-- s 28(1): no shares of the class are held, so no proportion is defined.
#ASSERT `How many of the offered shares do I have a pre-emptive right to acquire` 100 10 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 28(1): no shares shall be issued unless first offered.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the corporation issue these shares of the class without first offering them to the shareholders` TRUE `any other issue of shares` FALSE)
-- s 28(1): first offered to the shareholders at the price and on the terms offered to others.
#ASSERT `May the corporation issue these shares of the class without first offering them to the shareholders` TRUE `any other issue of shares` TRUE
-- s 28(2)(b): no pre-emptive right in a share dividend.
#ASSERT `May the corporation issue these shares of the class without first offering them to the shareholders` TRUE `shares to be issued as a share dividend` FALSE
-- s 28(1): the articles do not provide a pre-emptive right.
#ASSERT `May the corporation issue these shares of the class without first offering them to the shareholders` FALSE `any other issue of shares` FALSE
-- Hal's corporation issues warrants and options.
-- s 29(1)(a): in the certificates, warrants or other evidences.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation set out the conditions of its options and conversion rights where the Act requires` TRUE FALSE
-- s 29(1)(b): or in the certificates evidencing the securities they are attached to.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation set out the conditions of its options and conversion rights where the Act requires` FALSE TRUE
-- s 29(1): the conditions are set out in neither place.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation set out the conditions of its options and conversion rights where the Act requires` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 29(2).
#ASSERT `May my corporation make this conversion privilege option or right transferable or non-transferable` `a conversion privilege`
-- s 29(2).
#ASSERT `May my corporation make this conversion privilege option or right transferable or non-transferable` `an option`
-- s 29(2).
#ASSERT `May my corporation make this conversion privilege option or right transferable or non-transferable` `a right to acquire securities of the corporation`
-- s 29(2): options and rights to acquire may be made separable or inseparable.
#ASSERT `May my corporation make this option or right separable or inseparable from the securities it is attached to` `an option` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 29(2).
#ASSERT `May my corporation make this option or right separable or inseparable from the securities it is attached to` `a right to acquire securities of the corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 29(2) names options and rights to acquire for separability, not conversion privileges.
#ASSERT `May my corporation make this option or right separable or inseparable from the securities it is attached to` `a conversion privilege` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 29(3): 1000 authorized less 800 issued leaves exactly 200 to meet the exercise.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation reserved enough authorized shares to meet the exercise of its conversion privileges options and rights` TRUE 1000 800 200
-- s 29(3): 201 are needed and 200 remain.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has my corporation reserved enough authorized shares to meet the exercise of its conversion privileges options and rights` TRUE 1000 800 201)
-- s 29(3): the duty arises only if the articles limit the authorized shares.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation reserved enough authorized shares to meet the exercise of its conversion privileges options and rights` FALSE 0 800 5000
-- s 29.1(1).
#ASSERT `Is my corporation forbidden to issue this document in bearer form` TRUE TRUE
-- s 29.1(1): not in bearer form.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation forbidden to issue this document in bearer form` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 29.1(1): not a certificate, warrant or other evidence of such a right.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation forbidden to issue this document in bearer form` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 29.1(2): on the request of a holder of a bearer-form document issued before s 29.1 came into force.
#ASSERT `Must the corporation exchange my bearer-form certificate for a registered one when I ask` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 29.1(2): only on request.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the corporation exchange my bearer-form certificate for a registered one when I ask` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 29.1(2): the document was issued after s 29.1 came into force.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the corporation exchange my bearer-form certificate for a registered one when I ask` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§§ `The corporation holding or buying its own shares (Part V, s 30 to s 37)`

-- Ian's corporation holds shares in itself as a personal representative; Jo's holds them as security for a loan.
-- s 31(1): in the capacity of a personal representative, unless it or a related body corporate has a beneficial interest.
#ASSERT `May my corporation hold shares in itself as a personal representative` TRUE FALSE
-- s 31(1): a beneficial interest in the shares defeats the exception.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation hold shares in itself as a personal representative` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 31(1): not held as a personal representative.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation hold shares in itself as a personal representative` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 31(2): by way of security for a transaction in the ordinary course of a lending business.
#ASSERT `May my corporation hold shares in itself by way of security` TRUE TRUE
-- s 31(2): the transaction is not in the ordinary course of a lending business.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation hold shares in itself by way of security` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 31(2): not held by way of security.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation hold shares in itself by way of security` FALSE TRUE)
-- Kim's corporation holds shares to qualify for a licence that requires Canadian ownership.
-- s 32(1)(a): not constrained for that purpose.
#ASSERT `May my corporation hold shares in itself to meet a Canadian ownership requirement` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 32(1)(b): converted shares that are constrained and were not previously held.
#ASSERT `May my corporation hold shares in itself to meet a Canadian ownership requirement` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- s 32(1): neither paragraph (a) nor (b).
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation hold shares in itself to meet a Canadian ownership requirement` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 32(1) is "subject to subsection 39(8)": two years have run with the corporation still holding the shares.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation hold shares in itself to meet a Canadian ownership requirement` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 32(1): the purpose must be the Canadian ownership qualification.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation hold shares in itself to meet a Canadian ownership requirement` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Lou asks whether his corporation may hold shares in itself at all.
-- s 30(1)(a) with the exception in s 31(1).
#ASSERT `May my corporation hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 30(1)(a) with the exception in s 31(2).
#ASSERT `May my corporation hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 30(1)(a) with the exception in s 32(1).
#ASSERT `May my corporation hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 30(1)(a): a corporation shall not hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Mae's subsidiary wants to acquire shares of Mae's corporation.
-- s 31(3)(a): in its capacity as a personal representative, unless it would have a beneficial interest.
#ASSERT `May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation as a personal representative or by way of security` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 31(3)(a): the subsidiary would have a beneficial interest.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation as a personal representative or by way of security` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 31(3)(b): by way of security in the subsidiary's ordinary lending business.
#ASSERT `May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation as a personal representative or by way of security` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- s 31(3)(b): not in the ordinary course of a lending business.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation as a personal representative or by way of security` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 31(4): through issuance by the corporation to the subsidiary, if the prescribed conditions are met before the acquisition.
#ASSERT `May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation through their issuance to it` TRUE TRUE
-- s 31(4): the prescribed conditions were not met first.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation through their issuance to it` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 31(4): the acquisition is not by issuance from the corporation.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation through their issuance to it` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 31(5).
#ASSERT `Are the conditions that must be met after a subsidiary's acquisition by issuance satisfied` TRUE TRUE
-- s 31(5): the prescribed conditions are not met.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the conditions that must be met after a subsidiary's acquisition by issuance satisfied` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 31(5): no acquisition took place under the purported authority of subsection (4), so nothing is required.
#ASSERT `Are the conditions that must be met after a subsidiary's acquisition by issuance satisfied` FALSE FALSE
-- s 31(6)(b)(i): a condition prescribed for subsection (4) was not met.
#ASSERT `Do the prescribed consequences apply to my subsidiary's acquisition of shares of the corporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 31(6)(b)(ii): a condition prescribed for subsection (5) is not met or ceases to be met.
#ASSERT `Do the prescribed consequences apply to my subsidiary's acquisition of shares of the corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- s 31(6): all the conditions were met.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the prescribed consequences apply to my subsidiary's acquisition of shares of the corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 31(6)(a): the corporation did not permit the acquisition under the purported authority of subsection (4).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the prescribed consequences apply to my subsidiary's acquisition of shares of the corporation` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 30(1)(b) with the exception in s 31(3).
#ASSERT `May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- s 30(1)(b) with the exception in s 31(4).
#ASSERT `May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- s 30(1)(b): the s 31(4) conditions were not met.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 30(1)(b): a corporation shall not permit a subsidiary to acquire its shares.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Ned's subsidiary became a subsidiary on 1 March 2026 and is holding shares of the parent that section 31 does not allow.
-- s 30(2)(a): within five years from the date the body corporate became a subsidiary.
#ASSERT `By what day must my corporation's subsidiary dispose of the shares it holds in the corporation` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2031 3 1)
-- s 30(2)(b): five years from the date the corporation was continued -- the later of the two dates (fork cb1-F8).
#ASSERT `By what day must my corporation's subsidiary dispose of the shares it holds in the corporation` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 6 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2032 6 1)
-- s 30(2) is "subject to section 31": where s 31 permits the holding there is no duty to dispose.
#ASSERT `By what day must my corporation's subsidiary dispose of the shares it holds in the corporation` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Olly's corporation holds shares under the Canadian ownership exception and wants to transfer them.
-- s 32(2): satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the transfer would assist.
#ASSERT `May my corporation transfer shares it holds under the Canadian ownership exception` TRUE
-- s 32(2): shall not transfer unless so satisfied.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation transfer shares it holds under the Canadian ownership exception` FALSE)
-- s 32(3): without reasonable cause, fails to comply with subsection (2).
#ASSERT `Is my corporation guilty of an offence for transferring such shares without being satisfied` TRUE FALSE
-- s 32(3): reasonable cause.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation guilty of an offence for transferring such shares without being satisfied` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 32(3): no failure to comply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation guilty of an offence for transferring such shares without being satisfied` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 32(4): a director who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced is a party to and guilty of the offence.
#ASSERT `Am I as a director guilty of the offence my corporation committed under subsection 32(3)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 32(4): not knowingly.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I as a director guilty of the offence my corporation committed under subsection 32(3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 32(4): the person is not a director.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I as a director guilty of the offence my corporation committed under subsection 32(3)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 32(4): the corporation did not commit an offence under subsection (3).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I as a director guilty of the offence my corporation committed under subsection 32(3)` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 32(5): as if the transfer were an issue.
#ASSERT `Are the rules on the issue of shares applied to my corporation's transfer of shares it held under subsection 32(1)` TRUE TRUE
-- s 32(5): the shares are not transferred.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are the rules on the issue of shares applied to my corporation's transfer of shares it held under subsection 32(1)` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 32(6): not void, voidable or null solely because it contravenes subsection (2).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a transfer of shares by my corporation void or voidable just because it contravenes subsection 32(2)` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 32(6) does not save a transfer void on another ground.
#ASSERT `Is a transfer of shares by my corporation void or voidable just because it contravenes subsection 32(2)` TRUE TRUE
-- s 32(6): nothing makes the transfer void.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a transfer of shares by my corporation void or voidable just because it contravenes subsection 32(2)` FALSE FALSE)
-- Pat's corporation holds shares in itself and the directors want to vote them.
-- s 33(1): held as a personal representative and section 153 complied with.
#ASSERT `May my corporation vote or permit to be voted shares it holds in itself` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 33(1)(b): section 153 has not been complied with.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation vote or permit to be voted shares it holds in itself` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 33(1)(a): not held as a personal representative.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation vote or permit to be voted shares it holds in itself` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 33(2): the subsidiary satisfies the requirements of subsection (1).
#ASSERT `May my corporation permit its subsidiary to vote shares of the corporation` TRUE TRUE
-- s 33(2): the subsidiary does not satisfy them.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation permit its subsidiary to vote shares of the corporation` TRUE FALSE)
-- Quin's corporation has assets worth $1,000 after a proposed payment, liabilities of $600 and stated capital of $400.
-- s 34(2)(b): assets are not less than liabilities plus stated capital (1,000 = 600 + 400).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation forbidden to pay to acquire its own shares` FALSE 1000 600 400 FALSE)
-- s 34(2)(b): 999 is less than 1,000.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation forbidden to pay to acquire its own shares` FALSE 999 600 400 FALSE
-- s 34(2)(a): reasonable grounds for believing it is unable to pay its liabilities as they become due.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation forbidden to pay to acquire its own shares` TRUE 5000 600 400 FALSE
-- s 26(11) with s 34(2): an open-end mutual fund has no stated capital for this test (fork cb1-F9) -- 600 is not less than 600.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation forbidden to pay to acquire its own shares` FALSE 600 600 400 TRUE)
-- s 34(2)(b) for an open-end mutual fund: 599 is less than liabilities of 600.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation forbidden to pay to acquire its own shares` FALSE 599 600 400 TRUE
-- s 34(1): subject to its articles and subsection (2) -- neither stands in the way.
#ASSERT `May my corporation purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it` FALSE FALSE 1000 600 400 FALSE
-- s 34(1): the articles forbid the acquisition.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it` TRUE FALSE 1000 600 400 FALSE)
-- s 34(2): the realizable value test fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it` FALSE FALSE 999 600 400 FALSE)
-- s 34(2)(a): unable to pay its liabilities as they become due.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it` FALSE TRUE 5000 600 400 FALSE)
-- Rob's corporation wants to settle a claim by buying back shares; its assets would be $900, liabilities $600, and $300 is owed on shares ranking ahead.
-- s 35(1)(a): despite s 34(2), subject to s 35(3) -- 1,000 is not less than 600 + 300.
#ASSERT `May my corporation acquire its own shares for this purpose despite the general limit` `to settle or compromise a debt or claim asserted by or against the corporation` FALSE FALSE 1000 600 300
-- s 35(3)(b): 899 is less than 600 + 300.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation acquire its own shares for this purpose despite the general limit` `to settle or compromise a debt or claim asserted by or against the corporation` FALSE FALSE 899 600 300)
-- s 35(1): "subject to ... its articles".
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation acquire its own shares for this purpose despite the general limit` `to settle or compromise a debt or claim asserted by or against the corporation` TRUE FALSE 1000 600 300)
-- s 35(1)(b).
#ASSERT `May my corporation acquire its own shares for this purpose despite the general limit` `to eliminate fractional shares` FALSE FALSE 1000 600 300
-- s 35(1)(c).
#ASSERT `May my corporation acquire its own shares for this purpose despite the general limit` `to fulfil the terms of a non-assignable agreement under which the corporation has an option or is obliged to purchase shares owned by a director, an officer or an employee of the corporation` FALSE FALSE 1000 600 300
-- s 35(2)(a): subject to neither the articles nor s 35(3) (finding in NOTES).
#ASSERT `May my corporation acquire its own shares for this purpose despite the general limit` `to satisfy the claim of a shareholder who dissents under section 190` TRUE TRUE 0 600 300
-- s 35(2)(b).
#ASSERT `May my corporation acquire its own shares for this purpose despite the general limit` `to comply with an order under section 241` FALSE FALSE 0 600 300
-- s 35 lists five purposes; any other purpose is not within it.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation acquire its own shares for this purpose despite the general limit` `any other purpose` FALSE FALSE 1000 600 300)
-- s 35(3)(b): 900 is not less than 600 + 300.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation forbidden to pay to acquire its shares for one of the s 35(1) purposes` FALSE 900 600 300)
-- s 35(3)(b): 899 is less than 900.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation forbidden to pay to acquire its shares for one of the s 35(1) purposes` FALSE 899 600 300
-- s 35(3)(a): unable to pay its liabilities as they become due.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation forbidden to pay to acquire its shares for one of the s 35(1) purposes` TRUE 5000 600 300
-- Sue's corporation wants to redeem redeemable shares at $10 each; the articles set the redemption price at $10.
-- s 36(1): at prices not exceeding the redemption price stated in the articles.
#ASSERT `May my corporation purchase or redeem redeemable shares at this price` TRUE 10 10 FALSE FALSE 1000 600 300
-- s 36(1): the price exceeds the redemption price.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation purchase or redeem redeemable shares at this price` TRUE 11 10 FALSE FALSE 1000 600 300)
-- s 36(1) speaks of redeemable shares.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation purchase or redeem redeemable shares at this price` FALSE 10 10 FALSE FALSE 1000 600 300)
-- s 36(1): subject to the articles.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation purchase or redeem redeemable shares at this price` TRUE 10 10 TRUE FALSE 1000 600 300)
-- s 36(2)(b): 899 is less than 600 + 300.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation purchase or redeem redeemable shares at this price` TRUE 10 10 FALSE FALSE 899 600 300)
-- s 36(2)(b): not less than the aggregate.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation forbidden to pay to purchase or redeem redeemable shares` FALSE 900 600 300)
-- s 36(2)(b): less than the aggregate.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation forbidden to pay to purchase or redeem redeemable shares` FALSE 899 600 300
-- s 36(2)(a).
#ASSERT `Is my corporation forbidden to pay to purchase or redeem redeemable shares` TRUE 5000 600 300
-- s 37: a share surrendered as a gift (in Quebec, a legacy).
#ASSERT `May my corporation accept a share surrendered to it as a gift` TRUE
-- s 37: only a share surrendered as a gift.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation accept a share surrendered to it as a gift` FALSE)
-- s 37: only in accordance with section 38.
#ASSERT `May my corporation extinguish or reduce a liability for an amount unpaid on a share surrendered to it` TRUE TRUE
-- s 37: not except in accordance with section 38.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation extinguish or reduce a liability for an amount unpaid on a share surrendered to it` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 37: the corporation does nothing of the kind.
#ASSERT `May my corporation extinguish or reduce a liability for an amount unpaid on a share surrendered to it` FALSE FALSE

§§ `Reducing stated capital, adjusting it, dividends and shareholder liability (Part V, s 38 to s 45)`

-- Tom's corporation proposes a special resolution to distribute stated capital to the holders of a class. Its assets after the reduction would be worth $1,000 against liabilities of $600.
-- s 38(1)(b): by special resolution -- 67 of 100 votes is not less than two thirds; s 38(3) does not forbid it.
#ASSERT `May my corporation reduce its stated capital by special resolution for this purpose` `distributing to the holder of an issued share of any class or series of shares an amount not exceeding the stated capital of the class or series` 67 33 FALSE FALSE 1000 600
-- s 38(1): 66 of 100 votes is less than two thirds.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation reduce its stated capital by special resolution for this purpose` `distributing to the holder of an issued share of any class or series of shares an amount not exceeding the stated capital of the class or series` 66 34 FALSE FALSE 1000 600)
-- s 38(3)(b): the realizable value of the assets would be less than the liabilities.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation reduce its stated capital by special resolution for this purpose` `distributing to the holder of an issued share of any class or series of shares an amount not exceeding the stated capital of the class or series` 67 33 FALSE FALSE 599 600)
-- s 38(3)(b): assets equal to liabilities are not "less than" them.
#ASSERT `May my corporation reduce its stated capital by special resolution for this purpose` `distributing to the holder of an issued share of any class or series of shares an amount not exceeding the stated capital of the class or series` 67 33 FALSE FALSE 600 600
-- s 38(3)(a): reasonable grounds for believing the corporation would be unable to pay its liabilities as they become due.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation reduce its stated capital by special resolution for this purpose` `distributing to the holder of an issued share of any class or series of shares an amount not exceeding the stated capital of the class or series` 67 33 FALSE TRUE 5000 600)
-- s 38(3) does not limit a reduction for the purpose in paragraph (1)(c).
#ASSERT `May my corporation reduce its stated capital by special resolution for this purpose` `declaring its stated capital to be reduced by an amount that is not represented by realizable assets` 67 33 FALSE TRUE 0 600
-- s 38(1)(a), with a resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote (s 2(1) "special resolution").
#ASSERT `May my corporation reduce its stated capital by special resolution for this purpose` `extinguishing or reducing a liability in respect of an amount unpaid on any share` 1 0 TRUE FALSE 1000 600
-- s 38(1): "for any purpose including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing".
#ASSERT `May my corporation reduce its stated capital by special resolution for this purpose` `any other purpose` 67 33 FALSE FALSE 1000 600
-- s 38(1)(b): an amount not exceeding the stated capital.
#ASSERT `Is the amount my corporation distributes to a shareholder within the stated capital of the class or series` 400 400
-- s 38(1)(b): 401 exceeds 400.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the amount my corporation distributes to a shareholder within the stated capital of the class or series` 401 400)
-- s 38(2): it shall specify the stated capital account or accounts.
#ASSERT `Does our special resolution to reduce stated capital say what the Act requires` TRUE
-- s 38(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`Does our special resolution to reduce stated capital say what the Act requires` FALSE)
-- s 38(3)(b): assets not less than liabilities (and no stated capital term in this test).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation forbidden to reduce its stated capital for this purpose` `distributing to the holder of an issued share of any class or series of shares an amount not exceeding the stated capital of the class or series` FALSE 1000 600)
-- s 38(3)(b).
#ASSERT `Is my corporation forbidden to reduce its stated capital for this purpose` `distributing to the holder of an issued share of any class or series of shares an amount not exceeding the stated capital of the class or series` FALSE 599 600
-- s 38(3): "other than the purpose mentioned in paragraph (1)(c)".
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation forbidden to reduce its stated capital for this purpose` `declaring its stated capital to be reduced by an amount that is not represented by realizable assets` TRUE 0 600)
-- Una, a creditor, applies against Vic, a shareholder who was paid out of a reduction made contrary to section 38.
-- s 38(4)(b).
#ASSERT `Can a creditor apply to a court for an order against me as a shareholder who received something under a reduction of capital` `an order compelling a shareholder or other recipient to pay or deliver to the corporation any money or property that was paid or distributed as a consequence of a reduction of capital made contrary to section 38` TRUE TRUE
-- s 38(4)(a).
#ASSERT `Can a creditor apply to a court for an order against me as a shareholder who received something under a reduction of capital` `an order compelling a shareholder to pay to the corporation an amount equal to any liability of the shareholder that was extinguished or reduced contrary to section 38` TRUE TRUE
-- s 38(4) names two orders.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a creditor apply to a court for an order against me as a shareholder who received something under a reduction of capital` `any other order` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 38(4): only a creditor may apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a creditor apply to a court for an order against me as a shareholder who received something under a reduction of capital` `an order compelling a shareholder to pay to the corporation an amount equal to any liability of the shareholder that was extinguished or reduced contrary to section 38` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 38(4): the act must have been contrary to section 38.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a creditor apply to a court for an order against me as a shareholder who received something under a reduction of capital` `an order compelling a shareholder to pay to the corporation an amount equal to any liability of the shareholder that was extinguished or reduced contrary to section 38` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 38(5): not after two years from the date of the act complained of (counted by F1).
#ASSERT `By what day must an action to enforce a liability under section 38 be commenced` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2028 3 1
-- s 38(5): on the last day.
#ASSERT `Is an action to enforce a liability under section 38 in time` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2028 3 1)
-- s 38(5): after two years.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is an action to enforce a liability under section 38 in time` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2028 3 2))
-- Wes's corporation buys back 25 of the 100 issued shares of a class whose stated capital is $1,000.
-- s 39(1): 1,000 x 25 / 100 = 250.
#ASSERT `How much must my corporation deduct from the stated capital account when it acquires its own shares` 1000 25 100 EQUALS JUST 250
-- s 39(1): no shares were issued, so the proportion is not defined.
#ASSERT `How much must my corporation deduct from the stated capital account when it acquires its own shares` 1000 25 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 39(2): the payment is deducted from the account.
#ASSERT `What is the stated capital account balance after a payment to a shareholder under paragraph 241(3)(g)` 1000 300 EQUALS 700
-- s 39(3).
#ASSERT `Must my corporation adjust its stated capital accounts in accordance with our special resolution` TRUE
-- s 39(3): only a special resolution referred to in s 38(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my corporation adjust its stated capital accounts in accordance with our special resolution` FALSE)
-- s 39(4)(a): 1,000 x 25 / 100.
#ASSERT `How much must my corporation deduct from the stated capital account on a conversion or change of shares` 1000 25 100 EQUALS JUST 250
-- s 39(4)(a): no shares were issued.
#ASSERT `How much must my corporation deduct from the stated capital account on a conversion or change of shares` 1000 25 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 39(4)(b): the 250 deducted plus 40 additional consideration.
#ASSERT `How much must my corporation add to the stated capital account of the new class or series on a conversion or change of shares` 1000 25 100 40 EQUALS JUST 290
-- s 39(4)(b): the amount deducted under (a) is not defined.
#ASSERT `How much must my corporation add to the stated capital account of the new class or series on a conversion or change of shares` 1000 25 0 40 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 39(5).
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have two classes of interconvertible shares` TRUE TRUE
-- s 39(5): one class only is convertible.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation have two classes of interconvertible shares` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 39(5): two classes of shares.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my corporation have two classes of interconvertible shares` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 39(5): (600 + 400) / (60 + 40) = 10.
#ASSERT `How much stated capital is attributable to one of my corporation's interconvertible shares` FALSE 600 400 60 40 EQUALS JUST 10
-- s 39(5): "subject to its articles" -- the articles provide otherwise.
#ASSERT `How much stated capital is attributable to one of my corporation's interconvertible shares` TRUE 600 400 60 40 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 39(5): no issued shares, so the proportion is not defined.
#ASSERT `How much stated capital is attributable to one of my corporation's interconvertible shares` FALSE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 39(6): cancelled or, if the articles limit the number of authorized shares, may be restored.
#ASSERT `What becomes of shares my corporation has bought back redeemed or otherwise acquired` TRUE EQUALS `the shares must be cancelled or may be restored to the status of authorized but unissued shares of the class`
-- s 39(6): without such a limit, they are cancelled.
#ASSERT `What becomes of shares my corporation has bought back redeemed or otherwise acquired` FALSE EQUALS `the shares must be cancelled`
-- s 39(7).
#ASSERT `Is my corporation deemed not to have acquired shares it holds in itself under section 31` TRUE
-- s 39(7): shares not held as section 31(1) or (2) permits.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation deemed not to have acquired shares it holds in itself under section 31` FALSE)
-- s 39(8): still held at the expiration of two years -- deemed acquired at the expiration of the two years.
#ASSERT `On what day are the shares my corporation holds under paragraph 32(1)(a) deemed to have been acquired` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2028 3 1)
-- s 39(8): no longer held at the expiration of two years -- no deemed acquisition.
#ASSERT `On what day are the shares my corporation holds under paragraph 32(1)(a) deemed to have been acquired` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 39(8) speaks of shares held under paragraph 32(1)(a) (or converted and held under (b)).
#ASSERT `On what day are the shares my corporation holds under paragraph 32(1)(a) deemed to have been acquired` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 39(9).
#ASSERT `Do my shares become issued shares of the class or series they were converted or changed into` TRUE
-- s 39(9): shares not converted or changed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do my shares become issued shares of the class or series they were converted or changed into` FALSE)
-- s 39(10): increased by the number that became shares of another class or series.
#ASSERT `How many unissued shares does the first class have after a conversion or change` TRUE FALSE 200 50 EQUALS JUST 250
-- s 39(10): "unless the articles otherwise provide" -- the Act gives no figure then.
#ASSERT `How many unissued shares does the first class have after a conversion or change` TRUE TRUE 200 50 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 39(10): applies where the articles limit the authorized shares of the class.
#ASSERT `How many unissued shares does the first class have after a conversion or change` FALSE FALSE 200 50 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 39(11): not redeemed by reason only that the indebtedness is repaid.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are debt obligations redeemed just because the debt they evidence is repaid` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 39(11) does not stop redemption on another ground.
#ASSERT `Are debt obligations redeemed just because the debt they evidence is repaid` TRUE TRUE
-- s 39(12): may be reissued, pledged or hypothecated, subject to any applicable trust indenture or other agreement.
#ASSERT `May my corporation reissue pledge or hypothecate debt obligations it has acquired` FALSE
-- s 39(12): a trust indenture or agreement prohibits it.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation reissue pledge or hypothecate debt obligations it has acquired` TRUE)
-- s 39(12): the acquisition and reissue is not a cancellation of the debt obligations.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the acquisition and reissue of debt obligations a cancellation of them` TRUE)
-- Xan sold her shares to the corporation under a contract and has not been paid.
-- s 40(1): shall fulfil its obligations.
#ASSERT `Must the corporation fulfil its contract to buy my shares` FALSE
-- s 40(1): except if the corporation can prove enforcement would put it in breach of s 34 to 36.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must the corporation fulfil its contract to buy my shares` TRUE)
-- s 40(2): the claimant is entitled to be paid as soon as the corporation is lawfully able.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to be paid under my contract to sell my shares to the corporation` FALSE TRUE
-- s 40(2): the corporation is not yet lawfully able to pay.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to be paid under my contract to sell my shares to the corporation` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 40(2): the corporation has already fulfilled its obligations, so the status ends.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to be paid under my contract to sell my shares to the corporation` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 40(2): ranked subordinate to the rights of creditors.
#ASSERT `In a liquidation do I rank ahead of this person under my contract to sell shares to the corporation` `a creditor of the corporation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 40(2): subordinate to holders of a class whose rights were in priority.
#ASSERT `In a liquidation do I rank ahead of this person under my contract to sell shares to the corporation` `a holder of a class of shares whose rights were in priority to the rights given to the holders of the class of shares being purchased` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 40(2): but in priority to the rights of other shareholders.
#ASSERT `In a liquidation do I rank ahead of this person under my contract to sell shares to the corporation` `a holder of any other shares` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 40(2) ranks the claimant against three groups only.
#ASSERT `In a liquidation do I rank ahead of this person under my contract to sell shares to the corporation` `any other person` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 41: a reasonable commission in consideration of buying or procuring purchasers.
#ASSERT `May the directors authorize the corporation to pay a commission for the sale of its shares` TRUE TRUE
-- s 41: reasonable.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors authorize the corporation to pay a commission for the sale of its shares` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 41: only for buying, agreeing to buy, or procuring purchasers.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the directors authorize the corporation to pay a commission for the sale of its shares` TRUE FALSE)
-- Yvette's corporation proposes a dividend; assets after payment $1,000, liabilities $600, stated capital $400.
-- s 42(b): assets not less than liabilities plus stated capital.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation forbidden to declare or pay a dividend` FALSE 1000 600 400 FALSE)
-- s 42(b): 999 is less than 1,000.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation forbidden to declare or pay a dividend` FALSE 999 600 400 FALSE
-- s 42(a): unable to pay its liabilities as they become due.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation forbidden to declare or pay a dividend` TRUE 5000 600 400 FALSE
-- s 26(11) with s 42: an open-end mutual fund has no stated capital for this test (fork cb1-F9).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my corporation forbidden to declare or pay a dividend` FALSE 600 600 400 TRUE)
-- s 42(b) for an open-end mutual fund: 599 is less than liabilities of 600.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation forbidden to declare or pay a dividend` FALSE 599 600 400 TRUE
-- s 43(1): in money, subject to s 42.
#ASSERT `May my corporation pay a dividend in this form` `in money` FALSE 1000 600 400 FALSE
-- s 43(1) "subject to section 42": the solvency test fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation pay a dividend in this form` `in money` FALSE 999 600 400 FALSE)
-- s 43(1): in property, subject to s 42.
#ASSERT `May my corporation pay a dividend in this form` `in property` FALSE 1000 600 400 FALSE
-- s 43(1): by issuing fully paid shares.
#ASSERT `May my corporation pay a dividend in this form` `by issuing fully paid shares of the corporation` FALSE 1000 600 400 FALSE
-- s 42 forbids "a dividend" without limit, so a share dividend is caught too (fork cb1-F10).
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation pay a dividend in this form` `by issuing fully paid shares of the corporation` FALSE 999 600 400 FALSE)
-- s 43(1) names three forms.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation pay a dividend in this form` `any other form` FALSE 1000 600 400 FALSE)
-- s 43(2): the declared amount of the dividend stated as an amount of money is added.
#ASSERT `How much must my corporation add to the stated capital account when it pays a dividend in shares` TRUE 500 EQUALS JUST 500
-- s 43(2) applies if shares are issued in payment of a dividend.
#ASSERT `How much must my corporation add to the stated capital account when it pays a dividend in shares` FALSE 500 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Zack, a shareholder, is told he is liable for the corporation's debts.
-- s 45(1): not liable, as shareholders, for any liability, act or default of the corporation.
#ASSERT `Am I as a shareholder protected from liability for the corporation's liabilities acts and defaults` `as a shareholder only`
-- s 45(1): except under s 38(4).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I as a shareholder protected from liability for the corporation's liabilities acts and defaults` `under subsection 38(4)`)
-- s 45(1): except under s 118(4) or (5).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I as a shareholder protected from liability for the corporation's liabilities acts and defaults` `under subsection 118(4) or (5)`)
-- s 45(1): except under s 146(5).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I as a shareholder protected from liability for the corporation's liabilities acts and defaults` `under subsection 146(5)`)
-- s 45(1): except under s 226(4) or (5).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I as a shareholder protected from liability for the corporation's liabilities acts and defaults` `under subsection 226(4) or (5)`)
-- s 45(2): on a share registered in the shareholder's name for a debt of that shareholder to the corporation.
#ASSERT `May the articles give the corporation a lien or hypothec on my shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 45(2) is "subject to subsection 49(8)".
#ASSERT NOT (`May the articles give the corporation a lien or hypothec on my shares` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 45(2): the share must be registered in the name of the shareholder or their personal representative.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the articles give the corporation a lien or hypothec on my shares` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 45(2): for a debt of that shareholder to the corporation.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the articles give the corporation a lien or hypothec on my shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 45(3): in accordance with its by-laws.
#ASSERT `May the corporation enforce a lien or hypothec on my shares` TRUE TRUE
-- s 45(3): not in accordance with the by-laws.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the corporation enforce a lien or hypothec on my shares` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 45(3): there is no lien or hypothec under s 45(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`May the corporation enforce a lien or hypothec on my shares` FALSE TRUE)

§§ `Constrained shares sold by the corporation (Part VI, s 46 and s 47)`

-- Abel's corporation has constraints on who may own its shares for a Canadian ownership licence; some shares are held contrary to the constraints.
-- s 46(1)(a).
#ASSERT `May my corporation sell my constrained shares as if it were their owner` `to assist the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to qualify under a prescribed law of Canada or a province to receive licences, permits, grants, payments or other benefits by reason of attaining or maintaining a specified level of Canadian ownership or control` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 46(1)(b).
#ASSERT `May my corporation sell my constrained shares as if it were their owner` `to assist the corporation to comply with a prescribed law` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 46(1)(c).
#ASSERT `May my corporation sell my constrained shares as if it were their owner` `to attain or maintain a level of Canadian ownership specified in its articles` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- s 46(1) allows three purposes only.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation sell my constrained shares as if it were their owner` `any other purpose` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 46(1): the corporation must have constraints on its shares.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation sell my constrained shares as if it were their owner` `to assist the corporation to comply with a prescribed law` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 46(1): the shares must be owned (or determined by the directors to be capable of being owned) contrary to the constraints.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation sell my constrained shares as if it were their owner` `to assist the corporation to comply with a prescribed law` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 46(1): under the prescribed conditions and after the prescribed notice.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my corporation sell my constrained shares as if it were their owner` `to assist the corporation to comply with a prescribed law` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 46(2): in good faith, not unfairly prejudicial, not unfairly disregarding the holders taken as a whole.
#ASSERT `Have the directors selected the shares for sale as the Act requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 46(2): not in good faith.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have the directors selected the shares for sale as the Act requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 46(2): unfairly prejudicial.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have the directors selected the shares for sale as the Act requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 46(2): unfairly disregards the interests of the holders.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have the directors selected the shares for sale as the Act requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 46(3): the owner immediately before the sale is divested of their interest or right.
#ASSERT `Am I divested of my interest in my shares when the corporation sells them` TRUE
-- s 46(3): only where shares are sold under s 46(1).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I divested of my interest in my shares when the corporation sells them` FALSE)
-- s 46(3): the person who would otherwise be the registered owner.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to receive only the net proceeds of the sale of my shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 46(3): or a person who satisfies the corporation they could be treated as the registered holder under s 51.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to receive only the net proceeds of the sale of my shares` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- s 46(3): neither limb.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to receive only the net proceeds of the sale of my shares` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 46(3): the shares were not sold under s 46(1).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to receive only the net proceeds of the sale of my shares` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 46(3): the net proceeds with income earned, less taxes and the costs of administration of the trust fund: 1,000 + 20 - 50 - 30.
#ASSERT `How much am I entitled to receive from the sale of my shares` 1000 20 50 30 EQUALS 940
-- s 46(3): the net proceeds alone.
#ASSERT `How much am I entitled to receive from the sale of my shares` 1000 0 0 0 EQUALS 1000
-- s 46(4).
#ASSERT `Do subsections 51(4) to (6) apply to me as the person entitled to the proceeds of the sale` TRUE
-- s 46(4): only for the person entitled under s 46(3).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do subsections 51(4) to (6) apply to me as the person entitled to the proceeds of the sale` FALSE)
-- s 47(1): the proceeds of a sale under s 46(1) constitute a trust fund in the hands of the corporation.
#ASSERT `Do the proceeds of the sale of my shares form a trust fund held for me` TRUE
-- s 47(1): only proceeds of a sale under s 46(1).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the proceeds of the sale of my shares form a trust fund held for me` FALSE)
-- s 47(1): invested in the prescribed manner.
#ASSERT `Has the corporation invested the trust fund as the Act requires` TRUE
-- s 47(1).
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the corporation invested the trust fund as the Act requires` FALSE)
-- s 47(2): reasonable costs of administration.
#ASSERT `May the corporation deduct its costs from the trust fund held for me` TRUE
-- s 47(2): costs that are not reasonable.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the corporation deduct its costs from the trust fund held for me` FALSE)
-- s 47(3): a trust company in Canada registered as such under the laws of Canada or a province.
#ASSERT `May the corporation transfer the trust fund held for me to a trust company` TRUE
-- s 47(3): any other transferee.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the corporation transfer the trust fund held for me to a trust company` FALSE)
-- s 47(3): thereupon discharged of all further liability.
#ASSERT `Is the corporation discharged of liability for the trust fund held for me after transferring it` TRUE
-- s 47(3): no transfer, no discharge.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the corporation discharged of liability for the trust fund held for me after transferring it` FALSE)
-- s 47(4): a receipt signed by a person entitled under s 46(3).
#ASSERT `Is my signed receipt a complete discharge of the corporation and any trust company` TRUE
-- s 47(4): a receipt not signed by a person so entitled.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my signed receipt a complete discharge of the corporation and any trust company` FALSE)
-- s 47(5): ten years after the date of the sale (counted by F1).
#ASSERT `By what day must I claim the trust fund before it vests in the Crown` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2036 3 1
-- s 47(5): the ten years have not yet passed on the last day.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the trust fund held for me vested in the Crown on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2036 3 1))
-- s 47(5): unclaimed for ten years after the sale it vests in Her Majesty in right of Canada.
#ASSERT `Has the trust fund held for me vested in the Crown on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2036 3 2)
-- s 47(5): claimed, so it does not vest.
#ASSERT NOT (`Has the trust fund held for me vested in the Crown on this day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2040 1 1))
-- s 47(6).
#ASSERT `Do sections 3 to 5 of the Escheats Act apply to a trust fund that has vested in the Crown` TRUE
-- s 47(6): only a trust fund that vests under s 47(5).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do sections 3 to 5 of the Escheats Act apply to a trust fund that has vested in the Crown` FALSE)
